hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5401","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Aisha and Hafsa began the morning fasting, then food was gifted to them and they broke their fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in, and one of them asked him about that, and he said to them: Make up a day in its place. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, except Hammad ibn al-Walid. Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha."
"5402","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Mecca wearing a black turban. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham al-Dastuwai except Amr ibn al-Numan; Umar ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it. What is well known is from the hadith of Ammar al-Duhni and Hammad ibn Salama, from Abu al-Zubayr."
"5403","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bassam, a relative of Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib, reported to me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muhanna al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukayma, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he finished he turned to the people and said: Did any of you recite with me? They said: Yes. He said: I say, why is the Quran being contended with me. Yazid ibn Zuray said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani came to us before the plague in Basra and reported to us this hadith from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukayma, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar; then I heard it from Mamar."
"5404","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal, from Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Every Prophet has a legacy and dependents, and my legacy and dependents are the Ansar, so safeguard me concerning them. No one narrated this hadith from Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman except Ibn Abi al-Rijal; Umar ibn Hafs al-Ansari was alone in narrating it."
"5405","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Women used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then leave wrapped in their woolen garments. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Mughira ibn Muslim; Shababa was alone in narrating it. It is not narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"5406","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Suwayd al-Adawi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Arfaja ibn Burayh al-Ashjai, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out against my community while they are united, seeking to split their unity, kill him, whoever he may be. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Suwayd except Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib."
"5407","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib narrated to us, he said: Warqa ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see that your dreams have concurred that it is in the last ten, meaning the Night of Decree; so whoever among you seeks it should seek it in the last ten. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Warqa; Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib was alone in narrating it."
"5408","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Abi Hassan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talha al-Qannad narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. Then he entered his house and performed ablution, then came out and said: And upon you be peace. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Samura except with this chain; al-Fadl ibn Abi Hassan was alone in narrating it."
"5409","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa al-Mustamli narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif ibn Mazin narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by an oath along with a witness. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Mutarrif ibn Mazin."
"5410","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abu Rifaa Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Habib the judge narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Sulayman al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughira ibn Shuba, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his forelock, his turban, and his leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurra except Salm ibn Sulayman al-Dabbi."
"5411","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Kathir, the freedman of Samura, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three whom the angels do not approach: the one in major ritual impurity, the disbeliever, and the one perfumed with saffron. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir, the freedman of Samura, except Hisham, nor from Hisham except al-Mughira ibn Muslim; Shababa was alone in narrating it."
"5412","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abu Burayd al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be in my community the Mahdi; if shortened, seven years, otherwise eight, otherwise nine. My community shall enjoy therein a bliss they never enjoyed the like of. Allah shall send the sky upon them pouring, and the earth shall withhold nothing of vegetation, and wealth shall be piled up; a man shall stand and say: O Mahdi, give me, and he shall say: Take it. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Abu Burayd was alone in narrating it. Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb ibn al-Habhab and Yahya ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Ala ibn Bashir, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"5413","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy Prophets prayed in the mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa, upon him be peace; it is as if I see him wearing two Qatrani cloaks, in pilgrim sanctity upon a camel of the camels of Shanuah, bridled with a bridle of palm fiber, with two braids. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi was alone in narrating it."
"5414","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Jafar ibn Ayyash al-Kufi handed me his book, and I wrote from it: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Siyah, from his father, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Masruq, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of There is no god but Allah shall remain in good so long as they do not mind what is diminished of their worldly affairs in the matter of their religion; but when they do not mind what is diminished of their religion for the soundness of their worldly life, then There is no god but Allah shall be thrown back at them, and it shall be said to them: You are not truthful. This hadith is not narrated from Aisha except with this chain; Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar was alone in narrating it."
"5415","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Ayyash handed me his book, and I wrote from it: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, who said: Prayer was obligated as two units; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it in Mecca until he came to Medina, and he prayed it in Medina as long as Allah willed, then two units were added in the resident prayer, while travel prayer was left as it was. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar, and it is not narrated from Salman except with this chain."
"5416","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Ayyash handed me his book, and I wrote from it: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Aliya, from Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, the people rushed toward him, and I was among those who rushed. When I saw his face I knew it was not the face of a liar, and I heard him say: O people, feed food, spread peace, join kinship ties, and pray while people sleep; you shall enter Paradise in peace. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar, and none narrated it from Abu al-Aliya except Asim. What is well known is from the hadith of Awf al-Arabi, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Abdullah ibn Salam."
"5417","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Muhammad Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Masruq, that when he mentioned Aisha and reported from her he would say: The innocent one reported to me, declared innocent from above seven heavens, daughter of al-Siddiq, beloved of the Beloved of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhada except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, nor from al-Hasan except Abu Jabir; Abu Hatim was alone in narrating it."
"5418","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: my uncle Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by some twenty-odd degrees. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Qays, nor from Qays except Muhammad ibn al-Salt; Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj was alone in narrating it."
"5419","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aisha, that she said to him: Who killed Dhu al-Thudayya? Was it Ali ibn Abi Talib? He said: Yes. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A people shall emerge who recite the Quran, and it shall not pass their throats; they shall pass through religion as an arrow passes through game; their mark is a man with a deformed arm. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"5420","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from his father, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who clings to my practice when my community is corrupt shall have the reward of a martyr. No one narrates this hadith from Ata except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad; his son Abd al-Majid was alone in narrating it."
"5421","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Hutaym, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: I used to be startled at night, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am startled at night, so I take my sword, and I meet nothing but that I strike it with my sword. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you words taught to me by the Trustworthy Spirit? I said: Yes. He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which neither the righteous nor the wicked can surpass, from the evil of what descends from the sky and what ascends therein, from the evil of the trials of night and day, and from every nightly visitor except one who knocks with good, O Most Merciful. He said them, and it left him. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except al-Mughira ibn Muslim; Shababa was alone in narrating it."
"5422","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Shami narrated to us, he said: Murajim ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that Jarir ibn Abdullah entered the house while it was full and found no seat, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw to him his waist-wrapper or his cloak and said: Sit upon this. He took it, kissed it, held it to himself, and said: May Allah honor you, O Messenger of Allah, as you have honored me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Murajim; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn was alone in narrating it."
"5423","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Basri, who said: Yaqub ibn Ata narrated to us, from his father while he sat beside him, and Ata confirmed it from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O boy, guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pages have dried and the pens have been lifted. If the community strove to benefit you with something Allah did not decree for you, they could not do so; and if the community strove to harm you with something Allah did not decree against you, they could not do so. It is said that the Abu Amr from whom Ishaq al-Azraq narrated this hadith is Abu Amr ibn al-Ala, and Allah knows best. None narrated it from Abu Amr except Ishaq al-Azraq."
"5424","Muhammad ibn Harun Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad al-Bayruti: your father informed you, he said: my father informed me, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sabra al-Qurashi informed me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar reported to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that some people of Urayna came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Medina unhealthy for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: If you went out to our camels and drank of their milk and urine. They did so, and when they recovered they killed the shepherd of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), apostatized, and drove off the camels. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent in pursuit of them; they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra; al-Abbas ibn al-Walid was alone in narrating it from his father."
"5425","Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Jamil ibn al-Hasan al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafat, and when he said: Here I am, O Allah, here I am, he said: True good is the good of the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Mahbub ibn al-Hasan."
"5426","Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Uryan al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uttered the opening takbir with them in the dawn prayer, then gestured to them, then left and returned with his head dripping, and prayed with them, then said: I am only a man; I was in major ritual impurity and forgot. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abu al-Rabi was alone in narrating it."
"5427","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Bazzar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi the judge narrated to us, he said: al-Jahm ibn Waqid al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Habib ibn Abi Thabit say: I came to Abd Khayr al-Hamdani, who was the chief of police of Ali ibn Abi Talib, and when I entered to him he said: I heard Ali ascend the pulpit, praise Allah and extol Him, and say: O people, shall I not inform you of the best of this community after its Prophet? Abu Bakr; and the best of them after Abu Bakr is Umar; as for the third, had I wished to name him I would have named him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jahm ibn Waqid except Bishr ibn al-Walid and Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5428","Muhammad ibn Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aisha al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise shall enter Paradise hairless and white, curly-haired, with kohl-lined eyes, aged thirty-three, in the form of Adam, upon him be peace, sixty cubits tall within seven cubits. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammad ibn Salama, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"5429","Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Isa ibn Ibrahim ibn Isa ibn al-Mansur al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Isa ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Jafar al-Mansur, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abandoning a bequest is a disgrace in this world, and fire and shame in the Hereafter. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5430","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Aban al-Sarraj al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding in religion. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mamar; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad was alone in narrating it."
"5431","Muhammad ibn Malik ibn Dawud al-Shayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is an old man unable to perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, perform Hajj on behalf of your father. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Simak ibn Harb except Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi."
"5432","Muhammad ibn Habban ibn Bakr al-Bahili al-Basri narrated to us in Baghdad, he said: Kamil ibn Talha al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: A man said to Abu Hurayra: You have given us verdicts on everything, and you are about to give us verdicts even about defecation. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever draws a sword of enmity upon a path of the Muslims incurs the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Muhammad ibn Amr Abu Sahl al-Ansari; Kamil ibn Talha al-Jahdari was alone in narrating it."
"5433","Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Shayri al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Qurayr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no usury except in delay. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz except Muhammad ibn Thabit; al-Qawariri was alone in narrating it."
"5434","Muhammad ibn Hunayn al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck any of his wives, nor ever struck anything with his hand, except when striving in the cause of Allah. He was never wronged in anything and took revenge upon its doer, except when the sanctities of his Lord were violated, in which case he took revenge for Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Wail except Hisham ibn Urwa; Ali ibn Hashim was alone in narrating it."
"5435","Muhammad ibn Hunayn al-Attar narrated to us: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from his father, and from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you vomits during his prayer, or regurgitates, let him leave, perform ablution, then continue from what he already completed of his prayer, so long as he does not speak. Ibn Jurayj said: If he speaks, he repeats the prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"5436","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Awbad ibn Abi Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are asked: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill, say: The better and fuller of them. And if you are asked: Which of the two women did he marry, say: The younger of the two, she who came and said: O my father, hire him. He said: What did you see of his strength? She said: He lifted a heavy stone and threw it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Imran except his son Awbad, and it is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain."
"5437","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi al-Baghdadi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Khaythama, from al-Suddi, from Abu Umara al-Khaywani, from Ali, who said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not pass a stone or a tree but that it greeted him. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythama except Shuja ibn al-Walid, and none narrated it from al-Suddi except Ziyad ibn Khaythama and al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr."
"5438","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Khaythama, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of my community who has three daughters or three sisters whom he supports until they separate from him, except that he shall be with me in Paradise like this, joining his index and middle fingers. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythama except Shuja ibn al-Walid."
"5439","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythama narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Zayd ibn Ali, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of my community who has three daughters or three sisters and treats them well, except that they shall be a veil for him from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Ali except Abdullah ibn Isa, and none narrated it from Abdullah ibn Isa except Ziyad ibn Khaythama; Shuja ibn al-Walid was alone in narrating it."
"5440","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Umar ibn Rashid ibn Shajara al-Yamami narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, as I recall, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One religious community does not inherit from another, and the testimony of one religious community against another is not permitted, except my community, whose testimony against others is permitted. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Umar ibn Rashid."
"5441","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sulayman, from Aisha, who used to say: Order your husbands to wash from themselves the traces of urine and stool, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command that it be done. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn Utba."
"5442","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Abu Shayba Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the disbelievers, saying: Come to a word that is just between us and you, to the end of the verse."
"5443","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Abu Sufyan and his companions descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, he said to his companions: I saw in a dream that my sword Dhu al-Faqar broke, and that is a calamity; I saw cattle being slaughtered, and that is a calamity; and I saw myself wearing my armor, and that is your city, they shall not reach it, if Allah wills."
"5444","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr there were one hundred water-carrying camels, and with him were two horses; al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad rode one of them, while Musab ibn Umayr and Sahl ibn Hunayf took turns on the other. His companions took turns riding the water camels on the road, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ali, and Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, took turns on one water camel."
"5445","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Uzza was at Batn Nakhla, al-Lat was at al-Taif, and Manat was at Qudayd. Ali ibn al-Jad said: Batn Nakhla is the orchard of Banu Amir."
"5446","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray twenty units in Ramadan, plus the witr. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Hakam except Abu Shayba."
"5447","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Muaddib al-Basri al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand, and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sufyan ibn Husayn."
"5448","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini al-Baghdadi, Fustuqa, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qudama al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dhu al-Suwayqatayn of Abyssinia shall demolish the Kaba. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Sufyan ibn Uyayna."
"5449","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: Master of the Day of Judgment. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Yazid except Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"5450","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Nubayt ibn Umar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays forty prayers in my mosque, not missing a single prayer, Allah shall write for him freedom from the Fire and safety from punishment. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Nubayt ibn Umar; Ibn Abi al-Rijal was alone in narrating it."
"5451","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Salih ibn Malik al-Khwarizmi narrated to us, he said: Miswar ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: Do not say: The month has fallen short; we fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine days more often than we fasted thirty. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Miswar ibn al-Salt, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"5452","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Asadi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Maytham, from Burayda, who said: Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Kill the lone outcast, whoever among people he may be. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; Abbad ibn Yaqub was alone in narrating it."
"5453","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Salih ibn Maytham, from Burayda, from Ali, who said: al-Aswad Dhu al-Thudayya is cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Burayda, from Ali, except with this chain; Abbad ibn Yaqub was alone in narrating it."
"5454","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, that he saw a man leaving the mosque when the caller to prayer gave the call, and said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhada except Abu Hafs al-Abbar; Surayj ibn Yunus was alone in narrating it."
"5455","Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Ismail al-Alam al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakra, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: One whose life is long and whose deeds are good. He said: Which people are worst? He said: One whose life is long and whose deeds are evil. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hammad ibn Salama."
"5456","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui the judge narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Arara narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: I read in the book of my father in his handwriting, though I did not hear it from him, from Qatada, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There shall be in my community twenty-seven lying impostors, among them four women; and I am the seal of the Prophets, there is no Prophet after me. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Hisham al-Dastuwai; Muadh ibn Hisham was alone in narrating it. It is not narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain."
"5457","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Arara narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham handed us a book and said: This I heard from my father, so we wrote from it: from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered pilgrim sanctity after one of the two evening prayers. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Hisham al-Dastuwai; his son Muadh was alone in narrating it."
"5458","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Arara narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Hakam al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan report from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three destroy: obeyed miserliness, followed desire, and a man's admiration of himself out of arrogance; and three save: justice in pleasure and anger, moderation in wealth and poverty, and fear of Allah in secret and in public. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Humayd ibn al-Hakam; Muhammad ibn Arara was alone in narrating it."
"5459","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counseled me, saying: O Anas, perform ablution fully and your lifespan shall be increased; greet whomever of my community you meet and your good deeds shall multiply; when you enter your house, greet your household and the goodness of your house shall increase; pray the forenoon prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning; have mercy on the young and honor the elder, and you shall be among my companions on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ali ibn al-Jad, and none narrated it from Ali ibn al-Jad except Musaddad and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi."
"5460","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about bathing on Friday, and he said: Bathe."
"5461","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No pilgrim utters a glorification nor a magnification except that he is given glad tidings for it."
"5462","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two Umras expiate what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise. Hammad ibn Zayd said: I met Ubaydullah, and he reported to me from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5463","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father: Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Atiyya, from Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever purifies himself on Friday and performs purification well, then goes early to Friday prayer, neither speaking idly nor acting ignorantly, it shall be an expiation for him for what is between that Friday and the next. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Ismail ibn Hammad; Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba was alone in narrating it."
"5464","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father: from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic is He, hates the wealthy oppressor, the ignorant old man, and the needy arrogant one. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Ismail ibn Hammad; Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba was alone in narrating it."
"5465","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Mirthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A stone shall weigh as much as seven pregnant camels; it shall be thrown into Hell and fall therein for seventy autumns without reaching its bottom. No one narrated this hadith from Alqama ibn Mirthad except Muhammad ibn Aban, and it is not narrated from Burayda except with this chain."
"5466","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neighbor has the greatest right to his neighbor's preemption, and he shall be waited for if absent, when their path is one."
"5467","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5468","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to begin recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. None narrated these hadiths from al-Qasim ibn Man except Minjab."
"5469","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isa son of Maryam shall certainly traverse Fajj al-Rawha as a pilgrim or as one performing Umra."
"5470","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram reported to me, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr reported to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isa son of Maryam shall descend and remain among people for forty years."
"5471","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal shall not enter Medina, but shall alight at the trench; over every mountain pass thereof are angels guarding it. The first to follow him shall be women and slave girls; he shall go forth, the people shall follow him and turn him back, and he shall return angry until he alights at the trench; at that time Isa son of Maryam shall descend. None narrated these hadiths from Hisham ibn Urwa except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Uqba ibn Mukram was alone in narrating them."
"5472","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Imran ibn Abi Imran narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows the Book of Allah, Allah shall guide him from misguidance and protect him from an evil reckoning on the Day of Resurrection; that is because Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: Whoever follows My guidance shall neither go astray nor suffer."
"5473","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father: from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while rich beyond need of begging shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with scratches upon his face. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba."
"5474","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Abu Salama, from Muayqib ibn Abi Fatima, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May a man level the pebbles while praying? He said: If it must be, then once."
"5475","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Abu Qilaba, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any harm shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"5476","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, that Abu Dharr took his stipend and went with the servant to buy his needs from the market, then bought copper coins with what remained and gave them in charity, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever ties up gold or silver and does not spend it in the cause of Allah, it shall be embers on the Day of Resurrection with which he shall be branded."
"5477","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Abu Bishr, from Usayr ibn Ahmar, that Abu Dharr al-Ghifari entered the mosque and bowed hastily, so I said: I do not think this old man knows what he prays. He finished and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a single prostration but that Allah raises him a degree thereby and writes a good deed for him thereby."
"5478","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Yazid ibn Muattib, the freedman of Safiyya, from Safiyya bint Huyayy, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while before her was a heap of date stones, and asked her: What is this? She said: I glorify Allah with them, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Since I left you I have glorified more than everything you have glorified. She said: What did you say? He said: I said: Glory be to Allah, to the number of what He created. None narrated these hadiths from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan except Mustalim ibn Said; Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba was alone in narrating them."
"5479","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The king of the east shall march against the king of the west and kill him; then the king of the west shall march against the king of the east and kill him; then an army shall be sent against Medina and swallowed by the earth; then an army shall be sent and shall take captive some people of Medina; then a fugitive shall seek refuge at the sanctuary, and people shall gather to him like scattered birds coming to water, until three hundred and fourteen gather to him, among them women; he shall prevail over every tyrant and son of a tyrant, and such justice shall appear that the living shall wish their dead could see it. He shall live seven years; if he exceeds by an hour, then fourteen; then what is beneath the earth shall be better than what is above it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jafar ibn Ali except al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym; al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad was alone in narrating it."
"5480","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The last funeral the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over, he uttered four takbirs over it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nadr Abu Umar except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Uqba ibn Mukram was alone in narrating it. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"5481","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from his father Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then the fourth is the vilest, until the Hour comes. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Awdi except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Uqba ibn Mukram was alone in narrating it."
"5482","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever shall be reckoned on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, so that he shall say: O Lord, grant me rest, even to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Uqba ibn Mukram was alone in narrating it."
"5483","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Anbas Said ibn Kathir narrated to us, from his father Kathir ibn Ubayd, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah shall settle the dues of people on the Day of Resurrection, some from others, even the hornless sheep from the horned one, to the extent it wronged it."
"5484","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us, he said: Abu Junada al-Saluli narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection some people shall be ordered to Paradise; when they draw near it, smell its fragrance, look at its palaces and what Allah has prepared therein for its people, they shall be called: Turn them away from it; they have no share in it. They shall return with a regret the like of which the earliest never returned with, saying: O our Lord, had You admitted us to the Fire before showing us what we saw of Your reward and what You prepared therein for Your allies, it would have been easier for us. He said: That is what I intended for you. When you were alone you openly confronted Me with grave sins; when you met people you met them humbly, showing people other than what you give Me of your hearts. You feared people and did not fear Me; you honored people and did not honor Me; you abandoned for people and did not abandon for Me. Today I show you painful punishment along with depriving you of reward. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Junada al-Saluli."
"5485","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyya al-Saffar narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry off a woman, the first has the greater right. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Yusuf ibn Atiyya; Ahmad ibn Tariq was alone in narrating it."
"5486","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us: my father reported to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five harmful animals are all to be killed in the sacred and non-sacred lands: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"5487","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us: my father reported to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to depart on the day of sacrifice, but Safiyya menstruated. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Will you detain us? I said: She already performed both circuits of the coming together and circumambulated. He said: Then let her depart. None narrated these two hadiths from Ismail ibn Umayya except Ibn Abi Layla; Muhammad ibn Imran was alone in narrating them from his father."
"5488","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Arzami narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall all enter Paradise together, every one of you, except one who strays from Allah as a camel strays. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malik al-Ashjai except Sharik; Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Arzami was alone in narrating it."
"5489","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, said: Son of Adam, so long as you supplicate to Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you; were you to come to Me with the earth full of sins, I would meet you with the earth full of forgiveness, so long as you associate nothing with Me; were your sins to reach the clouds of the sky, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Qays ibn al-Rabi; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini was alone in narrating it."
"5490","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ubada ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Abu Wail, from Qays ibn Abi Gharaza, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, and we were called brokers, and said to us: O company of merchants, oaths and Satan attend this selling of yours, so mix it with charity. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Maryam; Ubada ibn Ziyad was alone in narrating it."
"5491","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wail ibn Hujr, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he bowed place his hands upon his knees and spread his fingers. No one narrated it except Qays ibn al-Rabi."
"5492","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: When Ibn Umar wanted to touch the Stone he would say: O Allah, with faith in You, belief in Your Book, and the practice of Your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he would invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and touch it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Muhajir except Awn ibn Sallam."
"5493","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the lowest heaven see the people of Illiyyun as the people of the world see a rising star on the horizon of the sky; Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how blessed. I said to Atiyya: What is meant by blessed? He said: Prosperous."
"5494","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you, as sacred as this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Musa ibn Uthman, and it is not narrated from al-Bara and Zayd ibn al-Arqam except with this chain."
"5495","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Hudhayfa asked a landowner for a drink, and he gave him drink in a silver vessel, so he threw it away, saying: Had I not warned him once or twice I would not have done so; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to drink from gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade, for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, nor from Fudayl except his son; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai was alone in narrating it."
"5496","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Barrad al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: my grandfather Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Najiya ibn Kab, from Ali, who said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your misguided uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him. I said: Shall I bury him while he is a misguided disbeliever? He said: Go and bury your father, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I went and buried him, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was dusty. He said: Go and wash, then I came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications for which I would not love to have such-and-such in exchange. No one narrated this hadith from Furat al-Qazzaz except his son al-Hasan, nor from al-Hasan except his son Ziyad."
"5497","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main reported to me, he said: Ismail ibn Mujalid reported to me, from his father, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I entered the house and found a devil behind the door, so I strangled him until I felt the cold of his tongue upon my hands; were it not for the supplication of the righteous servant, he would have remained tied up in the morning for people to see. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except his son Ismail, and none narrated it from al-Shabi except Mujalid."
"5498","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayda al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a lighter prayer than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while complete. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Abdullah except Hisham ibn Hassan, nor from Hisham except Abu Ubayda; Yahya ibn Main was alone in narrating it."
"5499","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub report from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Saba, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Fadala ibn Ubayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grows a white hair in the cause of Allah, it shall be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. A man said to him: Some men pluck white hair. He said: Whoever wishes may pluck his white hair, or he said: his light. This hadith is not narrated from Fadala ibn Ubayd except with this chain; Wahb ibn Jarir was alone in narrating it."
"5500","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayda al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Muhtasib ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When shall I meet my brothers? They said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers? He said: You are my companions; my brothers are those who believe in me though they never saw me. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Muhtasib ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abu Ubayda al-Haddad was alone in narrating it."
"5501","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They should not be both frequent cursers and truthful ones. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Qays; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini was alone in narrating it."
"5502","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Farwa ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Marzuban Abu Sad, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Over what does the highest assembly dispute? He said: Over expiations and ranks. As for ranks: feeding food, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep. As for expiations: performing ablution fully in cold weather, carrying feet to congregations, and waiting for one prayer after another. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sad al-Baqqal except al-Qasim ibn Malik; Ibn Abi al-Maghra was alone in narrating it."
"5503","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Habiba, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of one who frees a slave after his death is like one who gives a gift after he is full. No one narrated this hadith from Idris al-Awdi except Abu Yahya al-Taymi."
"5504","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salim, a truthful man, narrated to us, he said: Ashath, cousin of al-Hasan ibn Salih, who was preferred over al-Hasan ibn Salih, narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Written upon the gate of Paradise: Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Ali is the brother of the Messenger of Allah, two thousand years before the heavens and the earth were created. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Ashath, cousin of al-Hasan ibn Salih, nor from Ashath except Yahya ibn Salim; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai was alone in narrating it."
"5505","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyya al-Awfi narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward a pillar in the mosque and preach leaning upon it. Aisha ordered that this pulpit of his be made for him. When he stood upon it and left his place by the pillar, the pillar moaned loudly when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his place, out of longing for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to it and embraced it, and when he embraced it the sound we heard subsided. I said: Did you hear it? He said: I heard it, and the people of the mosque heard it; it is one of the pillars next to the chamber. No one narrated this hadith from Atiyya except his son; Ahmad ibn Tariq was alone in narrating it."
"5506","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: Muawiya said: I never ceased to hope for the caliphate since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If you rule, do good. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Ismail ibn Muhajir."
"5507","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting: Said ibn Kathir Abu al-Anbas reported to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will hear from me? So I spread my garment, and when he finished I gathered it to myself; by the One in whose hand is my soul, I never forgot a single hadith of it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Anbas except Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba."
"5508","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: my uncle al-Qasim ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me a handful of pebbles. I handed him some, and he threw them in the faces of the people; none of the people remained but that his eyes were filled with pebbles. Then was revealed: You did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw. No one narrated this hadith from Simak ibn Harb except Sulayman ibn Qarm, nor from Sulayman except Yahya ibn Yala; al-Qasim ibn Abi Shayba was alone in narrating it."
"5509","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Hilal, the freedman of Ribi, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar; be guided by the guidance of Ammar; and hold to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd. In this hadith, none said: from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Hilal the freedman of Ribi, except Ibrahim ibn Sad."
"5510","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Malik ibn Anas, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, from his father, who said: Ali and Ibn Abbas spoke about temporary marriage with women, and Ali said to him: You are a confused man; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women during the Farewell Pilgrimage. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri except Abthar ibn al-Qasim; Said ibn Amr was alone in narrating it."
"5511","5505 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray after Fajr until the sun rises, nor after Asr until the sun sets, and a woman shall not travel for three days except with a mahram, and a woman shall not be married on top of her paternal aunt nor on top of her maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Ibn Abi Layla and Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai; Abu Shihab is alone in transmitting it from Ibn Abi Layla."
"5512","5506 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will surely bring out of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection people who never did any good at all, and will admit them to Paradise by His mercy after the intercession of those who intercede. No one narrated this hadith from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, except Ibn Abi Zinad."
"5513","5507 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will come out of the Fire and will be named in Paradise al-Jahannamiyyun, and they will call upon Allah to remove that name from them, so Allah will remove it from them; and when they come out of the Fire they will sprout as feathers sprout. This hadith is not narrated from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah except with this chain; Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra is alone in transmitting it."
"5514","5508 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to embrace her while she had a waist-wrapper up to her knees. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar; Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid is alone in transmitting it."
"5515","5509 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever in the Fire will be like Uhud."
"5516","5510 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us: Amr ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Paradise there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to the heart of a human being."
"5517","5511 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until al-harj increases among you - three times. They said: What is al-harj? He said: Killing. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Atiyyah except Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi."
"5518","5512 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from al-Bara, about: Say, by the bounty of Allah and by His mercy, in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather: he said: The bounty of Allah is the Quran, and His mercy is that He made you among its people. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Abu Malik al-Janbi."
"5519","5513 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Minhal al-Sukuni narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats this tree shall not come near our mosque. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak except Ishaq ibn Sulayman."
"5520","5514 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Tufayl Abu Sidan narrated to us, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali, that he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had spread a shamlah cloak, and he sat upon it, he and Fatimah and Ali and al-Hasan and al-Husayn; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took its edges and tied them over them, then said: O Allah, be pleased with them as I am pleased with them. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd ibn Tufayl except Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah; Minjab is alone in transmitting it."
"5521","5515 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale involving gharar. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sad except with this chain; Ismail ibn Abi al-Hakam is alone in transmitting it."
"5522","5516 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umarah al-Khathami narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was revealed about Ali: Indeed those who believe and do righteous deeds, the Most Merciful will make love for them. He said: Love in the hearts of the believers. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Rawq except Bishr ibn Umarah; Awn ibn Sallam is alone in transmitting it."
"5523","5517 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin, when he broke his fast, with dates. No one narrated this hadith from Raqabah except Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz; Yahya ibn Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"5524","5518 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Isa al-Absi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, in a raised report, he said: Allah created the Garden of Adn with His Hand, and created its fruits therein, and split its rivers therein, then looked at it and said: Speak. It said: Successful indeed are the believers. He said: By My Might and My Majesty, no miser shall be My neighbor in you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Hammad ibn Isa; Minjab is alone in transmitting it."
"5525","5519 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will come on the Day of Resurrection encircled around his neck with seven earths. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Ismail ibn Muslim; Abu Muawiyah is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"5526","5520 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah, and let whoever is with him say: May Allah have mercy on you, and let him say: May Allah guide you and set your affairs right. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except Hafs; Yahya al-Himmani is alone in transmitting it."
"5527","5521 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd, he said: Udaysah bint Uhban ibn Sayfi al-Ghifari narrated to me, from her father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you see two men of my ummah fighting each other over kingship, then take at that time a sword of wood and fight with it. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Rustum except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Ubayd ibn Yaish is alone in transmitting it."
"5528","5522 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Jassas, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq, he said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the top of the mountain and said: O sons of Abd Manaf, indeed I am a warner to you, indeed I am a warner to you. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad al-Jassas except al-Musayyab ibn Sharik; Uqbah ibn Mukram is alone in transmitting it."
"5529","5523 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr and al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I owe the freeing of a slave, and I have a black non-Arab slave girl. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring her to me. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: And do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Then free her. No one narrated this hadith from al-Minhal and al-Hakam except Ibn Abi Layla."
"5530","5524 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Ayyub Abi al-Ala, from Qatadah and al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit the hand of a man, so he pulled his hand from him and his front tooth fell out; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who invalidated it, then said: One of you eats the flesh of his brother as the stallion eats, or as the stallion bites. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah except Ayyub Abu al-Ala, nor from Ayyub except Yazid; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"5531","5525 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Maysarah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Hakim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to us while we were in Juhaynah, that we should not benefit from the carcass by using its skin nor its sinew. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Maysarah except Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah."
"5532","5526 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of this ummah is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. No one narrated this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan."
"5533","5527 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq ibn Sahl ibn Abi Khaythamah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: There was in my care a slave girl from the Ansar, so I married her off; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me on the day of her wedding and said: O Aishah, did you not sing for her? Will you not sing for her? For this clan of the Ansar loves singing. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah from Aishah except from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yunus ibn Bukayr is alone in transmitting it."
"5534","5528 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri and Ayyub ibn Bashir al-Ansari, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness: Pour over me water from seven waterskins, from different wells; so they did. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Bashir except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yunus ibn Bukayr is alone in transmitting it."
"5535","5529 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Ubaydillah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umrah, for they remove as the bellows removes the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hatim ibn Ismail."
"5536","5530 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sharecropping. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Abthar; Said ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"5537","5531 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The plague is martyrdom for my ummah, and the piercing of your enemies from the jinn; it comes out in the armpits and groins of men; the one who flees from it is like the one who flees from battle, and the one who is patient over it is like the fighter in the path of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar, from Aishah, except with this chain; Yusuf ibn Maymun is alone in transmitting it."
"5538","5532 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn Muhriz al-Qawariri narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he disliked that one should blow before him in prayer or in his drink. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Mahbub ibn Muhriz; Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"5539","5533 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Abdullah al-Faqih narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa al-Daqiqi narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Qays al-Araj al-Makki, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, he said: We were with Abu al-Darda returning from the summer campaign, and he said: O people, gather; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah will forbid the rest of his body to the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Sadaqah ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"5540","5534 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the market he said: O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from striking a sinful oath therein or a losing bargain. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Muhammad ibn Aban."
"5541","5535 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the last two rakahs the Opening of the Book. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Sinan ibn Harun."
"5542","5536 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash ibn al-Mutamir, he said: I saw Abu Dharr while he was holding the ring of the Kabah, saying: I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari; whoever does not know me, I am Jundub al-Ghifari; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of my Household is the example of the ship of Noah; whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it drowns."
"5543","5537 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abi al-Jahm, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept wiping both before the revelation of al-Maidah and after it until Allah took him. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Sawwar."
"5544","5538 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Salt al-Amiri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sharik, from Bishr ibn Ghalib, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Jibril, peace be upon him, descended upon him and said: O Muhammad, if it pleases you to worship Allah with His true worship, then say: O Allah, to You is praise, praise eternal with Your eternity, and to You is praise, praise everlasting with no end short of Your will, at every glance of an eye and breath of a soul. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Minjab is alone in transmitting it."
"5545","5539 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Mahbub narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid continuous fasting. We said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously? He said: I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord, Who feeds me and gives me drink. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"5546","5540 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhayb al-Nadr ibn Said ibn Shubrumah al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man whom Allah gives knowledge and then conceals it will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"5547","5541 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhayb al-Nadr ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The creation are the dependents of Allah, so the most beloved of people to Allah is the one who does good to His dependents. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Hakam except Musa ibn Umayr."
"5548","5542 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from al-Aswad and Shurayh al-Nakhai, they said: We entered upon Aishah asking her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embrace while fasting? We said to Alqamah: O Abu Shibl, you ask her. He said: I am not the one who would speak intimately to her today. Aishah said: What is the matter with you? They said: O Mother of the Believers, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embrace while fasting? She said: Yes, but he was the most in control of his desire among you. No one narrated this hadith except al-Ajlah, nor from al-Ajlah except Abu Usamah; al-Hasan ibn Sahl is alone in transmitting it."
"5549","5543 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a black slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A traveler passed by me while I was with the livestock of my master; may I give him milk from it without his permission? He said: No. He said: I shoot game, killing outright and wounding. He said: Eat what you killed outright and leave what you only wounded. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"5550","5544 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Yazid ibn al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, in a raised report, he said: There is no one more jealous than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and for that He forbade shameful acts, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi; Said ibn Khuthaym is alone in transmitting it."
"5551","5545 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, he said: Masadah ibn al-Yasa narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, that an old woman from the Ansar came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to admit me to Paradise. The Prophet of Allah said: Old women shall not enter Paradise. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went and prayed, then returned to Aishah, and Aishah said: She has met hardship and distress from your words. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is indeed so; when Allah admits them to Paradise He will turn them into virgins. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Abi Arubah."
"5552","5546 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim al-Abbadani narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Muslims who lose three of their children who have not reached puberty except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy upon them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan except Abu Asim al-Abbadani; Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi is alone in transmitting it."
"5553","5547 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim ibn Hilal al-Jufi narrated to us, from Salih al-Murri, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people who had hunted a gazelle and tied it to the pole of a tent. It said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given birth and I have two fawns; ask permission for me to suckle them, then I will return to them. He said: Where is the owner of this? The people said: We are, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her go until she goes to her two fawns to suckle them and comes back to you. They said: And who guarantees that for us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I do. So they released her, and she went and suckled, then returned to them, and they tied her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by them and said: Where are the owners of this? They said: Here we are, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Will you sell her? They said: O Messenger of Allah, she is yours. So they released her and set her free, and she went. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Salih al-Murri; Abd al-Karim ibn Hilal is alone in transmitting it."
"5554","5548 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel wrote a book, then followed it and abandoned the Torah. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Jandal ibn Waliq is alone in transmitting it."
"5555","5549 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Israil al-Mulai narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ali, he said: When the righteous are mentioned, then welcome Umar; we, the companions of Muhammad, peace be upon him, did not consider it unlikely that tranquility speaks upon the tongue of Umar."
"5556","5550 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Shabib al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man pray a prayer in which he does not complete its bowing and its prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab except his son Talhah, nor from Talhah except Ibn Abi Fudayk, nor from Ibn Abi Fudayk except Ibn Abi Uways; Abdullah ibn Shabib is alone in transmitting it."
"5557","5551 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ghazwan ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him take a bath. No one narrates this hadith from al-Amash except Shayban, nor from Shayban except Ubaydullah; Ismail ibn Ghazwan is alone in transmitting it."
"5558","5552 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse time, for Allah is time. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and none narrated it from Sufyan except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii and Asad ibn Musa."
"5559","5553 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray in the resting places of camels, and pray in the folds of sheep. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Yunus ibn Bukayr."
"5560","5554 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave after it was buried. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Abu Sinan, and Mihran is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain."
"5561","5555 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi and said takbir over him four times. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, except Abdah; Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz is alone in transmitting it. And Sufyan al-Thawri and Abdah narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah."
"5562","5556 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and his companions camped for rest, and nothing woke them but the sun. He stood and ordered the caller to prayer, who called the adhan and the iqamah, and he prayed. Masruq said: I would not love to have the world and all it contains in place of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after sunrise. No one narrated this hadith from Masruq except Tamim ibn Salamah, nor from Tamim except Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad; Abidah ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it. Masruq did not narrate any hadith from Ibn Abbas other than this."
"5563","5557 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting merchandise on the way before it is brought down to the markets. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Muadh ibn Muhammad; al-Muqaddami is alone in transmitting it."
"5564","5558 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yunus al-Lului narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned to him on the day of Hunayn three shares: one share for him and two shares for his horse. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Abu Muawiyah; Hisham ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5565","5559 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: nor of those who go astray, he said: Amin, raising his voice with it. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad; Dirar ibn Surad is alone in transmitting it."
"5566","5560 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked his sacrificial animal and garlanded it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab except Qays, nor from Qays except Waki; Sufyan ibn Waki is alone in transmitting it."
"5567","5561 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and the wage of a prostitute. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibn Abi Layla; al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad is alone in transmitting it."
"5568","5562 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Musarrif ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers on a journey. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad except Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"5569","5563 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Umar ibn Qays; Ahmad ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"5570","5564 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dhari narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Numan al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Qatan ibn Nusayr is alone in transmitting it."
"5571","5565 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Burdah, from Abi Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and witnesses. In the hadith of Abi Ishaq, from Abi Burdah, from Abi Musa, none said: and witnesses, except Abu Bilal al-Ashari, from Qays."
"5572","5566 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd Manaf, let me not know you preventing anyone who circumambulates the House from praying at any hour he wishes, of night or day. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla is alone in transmitting it."
"5573","5567 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Yaqub ibn Abi al-Mutayd, Abu al-Mutayd, narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mention, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to the noblest morals of this world and the Hereafter? That you join ties with one who cuts you, give to one who deprives you, and pardon one who wrongs you. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq except Yaqub ibn Abi al-Mutayd; his son Nuaym ibn Yaqub is alone in transmitting it."
"5574","5568 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from al-Hasan, from Anas, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard the sound of a bell, and said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Yusuf ibn Maymun; Ali ibn Mushir is alone in transmitting it."
"5575","5569 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Bakkar al-Sadi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Mamar ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it."
"5576","5570 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Zaidah Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Habib al-Qadi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then one of us would shoot his arrow and see where it landed. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Umar ibn Habib; Abu Zaidah is alone in transmitting it."
"5577","5571 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Umar al-Ahmasi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted is His remembrance, said: Whomever I deprive of his two precious things I shall compensate him for them with Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Husayn ibn Umar, and it is not narrated from Jarir except with this chain."
"5578","5572 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Dhayyal al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: A man said to al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Hayy: Shall I wipe over the two leather socks? He said: Yes. He said: If my Lord says to me: Who commanded you with this? He said: Say: al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Hayy. He said: If it is said to you, you? He said: I will say: Mansur ibn al-Mutamir commanded me. He said: If it is said to Mansur? He said: He will say: Ibrahim commanded me. He said: If it is said to Ibrahim? He said: He will say: Hammam ibn al-Harith commanded me. He said: If it is said to Hammam ibn al-Harith? He said: He will say: Jarir ibn Abdullah commanded me. He said: If it is said to Jarir? He said: He will say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Husayn ibn Dhayyal; Abu Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"5579","5573 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Atiyyah, from Abi Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about His saying: I shall force him to climb, he said: A mountain of fire in the Fire, he is charged to climb it; when he places his hand on it, it melts, and when he lifts it, it returns, and when he places his foot on it, it melts, and when he lifts it, it returns. None raised this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except Sharik, and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Ammar al-Duhni but stopped it as his own saying."
"5580","5574 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Atiyyah, he said: I heard Aba Said al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about this verse: Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in the life of this world and in the Hereafter - he said: In the Hereafter means in the grave. None raised this hadith from Musa ibn Qays except Qabisah; Uqbah is alone in transmitting it, and Abu Nuaym narrated it from Musa ibn Qays but stopped it as his own saying."
"5581","5575 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Sharik, and Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan and the people narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Bakr ibn Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5582","5576 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ubaydah ibn Sufyan, from Abi al-Jad al-Damri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abthar; Said ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ubaydah ibn Sufyan except with this chain."
"5583","5577 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, from Salman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: a gray-haired adulterer, a poor arrogant person, and a man to whom Allah gave merchandise, so he sells only with his oath and buys only with his oath. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hafs; Said ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Salman except with this chain."
"5584","5578 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Sharik; Minjab is alone in transmitting it."
"5585","5579 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We recited it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for years: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery - the verse - then was revealed: Except him who repents and believes. And I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoice with a joy more intense than his joy over it, and over: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abdullah ibn Raja al-Makki."
"5586","5580 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a single tawaf for his Hajj and his Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad."
"5587","5581 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abi al-Haytham, the owner of reeds, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abi Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Abi al-Haytham except Qays."
"5588","5582 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Yusuf al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the noble of a people comes to you, honor him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Husayn ibn Yusuf is alone in transmitting it."
"5589","5583 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Burayd al-Ashari narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love the Arabs for three reasons: because I am an Arab, the Quran is Arabic, and the tongue of the people of Paradise is Arabic. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Burayd; al-Ala ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"5590","5584 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Ata narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first whom the Truth will shake hands with after me is Umar, and the first whom He will greet, and the first whom He will take by the hand and admit to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Kaysan except Dawud ibn Ata; Ismail al-Talhi is alone in transmitting it."
"5591","5585 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Umarah ibn Ruwaybah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They are the two decisive matters: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq except Muhammad ibn Aban, and it is not narrated from Umarah ibn Ruwaybah except with this chain."
"5592","5586 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eight rakahs at night and pray witr with three. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Waththab, except Abu Bakr al-Nahshali."
"5593","5587 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Qasim ibn Habib al-Tammar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah, from Abi Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two groups of my ummah have no share in Islam: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Amr ibn al-Qasim; Abdullah ibn Aban is alone in transmitting it."
"5594","5588 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: A man was struck by need and went out to the desert, and his wife said: O Allah, provide us with what we knead and what we bake. The man came back to find the bowl full of dough, in the oven the sides of roasted meat, and the millstone grinding. He said: Where is this from? She said: From the provision of Allah. Then he swept what was around the millstone, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he left it, it would have kept turning - or he said: grinding - until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Hisham ibn Hassan, nor from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ahmad ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"5595","5589 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the market he said: O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market, and I seek refuge in You from disbelief and sinful deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Muhammad ibn Aban, and it is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain."
"5596","5590 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you go barefoot, go barefoot with both feet together, and when you wear sandals begin with the right; when you take them off, take off the left. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Ali ibn Hakim."
"5597","5591 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most helpless of people is the one helpless in supplication, and the most miserly of people is the one miserly with greeting of peace. None narrated this hadith from Asim except Hafs; Masruq is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5598","5592 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ubayd, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Abi Harun, from Abi Said al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us wearing a cloak of sundus silk, and we had not seen him more handsome since a long time than on that day; then he stood up in alarm and took it off, then came out to us in a Hibarah cloak and said: Silk is the clothing of the people of Paradise; whoever wears it in this world shall not wear it in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Isa ibn Ubayd; Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah is alone in transmitting it."
"5599","5593 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn al-Rabi al-Usfuri narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no possessor of kinship who comes to his relative asking for some surplus that Allah gave him, and he is miserly toward him, except that Allah will bring out for him on the Day of Resurrection a snake from Hell called Shuja, licking its lips, and he will be collared with it. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Ishaq ibn al-Rabi al-Usfuri."
"5600","5594 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Talut ibn Abbad al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu Ghassan al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Sad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The sword of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was curved, and its pommel was of silver. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Sad except Yahya ibn Kathir."
"5601","5595 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dhari narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you ask his Lord for his need, even asking Him for the strap of his sandal when it breaks. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Jafar ibn Sulayman; Qatan ibn Nusayr is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5602","5596 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Bakkar al-Sughdi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib, from Abi Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh; their best follow their best, and their worst follow their worst. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Hazim except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib, nor from Abd al-Aziz except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Mamar ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sad except with this chain."
"5603","5597 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Bakkar al-Sughdi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from his maternal uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abi Barzah al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah except Abdullah ibn Amir, nor from Abdullah ibn Amir except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Mamar ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abi Barzah except with this chain."
"5604","5598 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take a bath with a sa and perform ablution with a mudd. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik except Sayf ibn Muhammad; Jumhur ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"5605","5599 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from his father, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw no harm in making up Ramadan during the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini is alone in transmitting it."
"5606","5600 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him, making the prostration lower than the bowing. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr; al-Shafii is alone in transmitting it."
"5607","5601 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, he said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet are Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except Muhammad ibn Jabir, nor from Muhammad ibn Jabir except Umar ibn Yunus; Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah is alone in transmitting it."
"5608","5602 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hayyaji narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he did not rise from his place until prayer became permissible. And he said: Whoever prays the morning prayer, then sits in his place until prayer becomes permissible for him, it will be like an accepted Umrah and Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq."
"5609","5603 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Matar al-Warraq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was at a well drawing water, Abu Bakr entered and drew one or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah forgave him. Then Umar came and drew, and I never saw a great man among the people drawing his drawing until the people watered their camels to satisfaction. No one narrated this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Ibn Zaidah; Ali ibn Said is alone in transmitting it."
"5610","5604 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abi Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go out to the expedition of Tabuk, he said to Jadd ibn Qays: O Jadd ibn Qays, what do you say about fighting the Banu al-Asfar? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man fond of women, and whenever I see the women of Banu al-Asfar I am tempted, so permit me to stay and do not tempt me. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And among them is he who says: Permit me and do not tempt me; unquestionably, into temptation they have fallen, and indeed Hell encompasses the disbelievers. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Rawq except Bishr ibn Umarah."
"5611","5605 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, he said: Abu Sad al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from an expedition he would say: Returning, repenting, if Allah wills, to our Lord giving praise. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Sad al-Baqqal except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri; Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi is alone in transmitting it."
"5612","5606 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say to the people when he married the daughter of Ali: Will you not congratulate me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every tie and lineage will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage. None transmitted this hadith well from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except al-Hasan ibn Sahl, and others narrated it from Sufyan, from Jafar, from his father, without mentioning Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"5613","5607 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lie about me; indeed whoever lies about me is daring. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, except Sharik; Abu Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"5614","5608 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is much, and those who act upon it are few. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, and none narrated it from Abu Khalid except al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal and Asad ibn Musa."
"5615","5609 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumani narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that there was a dog among the Children of Israel close to giving birth; her owners were visited by a guest, and she said: I shall not bark at our guest tonight. Her puppies howled in her belly, and it was revealed to a man among them: The example of this dog is the example of a nation that will come after you, whose foolish ones will dominate their scholars. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Shuayb ibn Safwan and Abu Awanah, and none narrated it from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Hammad."
"5616","5610 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumani narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There was a kid goat among the Children of Israel whom its mother nursed until satisfied; one day it strayed and suckled many sheep but was not satisfied. It was revealed to a man among them: The example of this kid is the example of a people who will come after you; a man will be given what suffices a nation or a tribe, yet he will not be satisfied. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Shuayb ibn Safwan and Abu Awanah, and none narrated it from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Hammad."
"5617","5611 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Tawus, from al-Hajuri Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning the umra gift that it is valid. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Amr ibn Dinar, well - as the people narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar - except Hammad ibn al-Jad; Hudbah ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it. And Muadh ibn Hisham narrated it from his father, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hajuri, from Ibn Abbas."
"5618","5612 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The first who shot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sad. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; al-Ala ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"5619","5613 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ata al-Bazzar, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you attains the reality of faith until he guards his tongue. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Hafs; Sufyan ibn Bishr is alone in transmitting it."
"5620","5614 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us and mix with us, and we had a young boy called Abu Umayr. He said: O Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do? No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah is alone in transmitting it."
"5621","5615 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Malih ibn Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sharik, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Aws, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who cut down the lote trees will be thrown into the Fire on their faces, thrown. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Sharik; Malih ibn Waki is alone in transmitting it, from his father."
"5622","5616 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abi Salih, from Abi Hurayrah - Sharik said: I do not know whether he raised it or not - he said: Leadership, its beginning is regret, its middle is liability, and its end is punishment on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Isa except Sharik; Muhammad ibn Aban is alone in transmitting it."
"5623","5617 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, that al-Husayn ibn Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed. This hadith is not narrated from al-Husayn ibn Ali except with this chain; Dirar ibn Surad is alone in transmitting it."
"5624","5618 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Mina, Qalun, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from al-Muthanna al-Qari, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is the dome of Islam, the abode of faith, the land of migration, and the place of the lawful and the unlawful. This hadith is not narrated from the Prophet, peace be upon him, except with this chain; Qalun is alone in transmitting it."
"5625","5619 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, and I said: I have no dislike for you, but I do not love to marry while my children are small. He said: Do you have anything else? I said: No. He said: The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh, the most affectionate to a small child, and the most careful with a husband regarding wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim is alone in transmitting it."
"5626","5620 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sayyar Abi al-Hakam, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Aishah, she said: I saw Jibril, peace be upon him, wearing a red turban, letting it hang between his shoulders. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except al-Darawardi."
"5627","5621 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Bilal al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bukayr al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is killed seeking thereby the Face of Allah, Allah will not punish him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Abdullah ibn Bukayr."
"5628","5622 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale involving gharar. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad; Dirar ibn Surad is alone in transmitting it."
"5629","5623 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to wash once every week - meaning Friday. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; Abu Hilal is alone in transmitting it."
"5630","5624 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Bakr ibn Wail, from Ubayd ibn Hasan, from Ibn Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his prayer: Our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"5631","5625 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from his father, from Bakr ibn Wail, from Abi Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his houses on his left; when he prayed the prayer, he turned to his houses to his left. No one narrated these two hadiths from Bakr ibn Wail except Yala ibn al-Harith, nor from Yala except his son; Abu Kurayb is alone in transmitting them."
"5632","5626 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that Allah expand his provision and extend his life, let him join his kinship. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Rushdayn ibn Sad."
"5633","5627 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Bakkar al-Sadi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Shubah, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gather both his parents for anyone except Sad; he said to him on the day of Uhud: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Mamar ibn Bakkar al-Sadi."
"5634","5628 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Abi Sad al-Baqqal, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Bakhtari, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every treacherous person there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection; the protection of the Muslims is one, the lowest of them strives for it; whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Sad al-Baqqal except Hashim; Dirar ibn Surad is alone in transmitting it."
"5635","5629 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Hakam ibn Awanah narrated to us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abi Awn, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abi Hurayrah, that when revelation descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would get a headache, so he would cover his head with henna. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn al-Musayyab except Abu Awn, nor from Abu Awn except al-Ahwas, nor from al-Ahwas except Sulayman ibn al-Hakam ibn Awanah; Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah is alone in transmitting it."
"5636","5630 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A banner will be raised for the treacherous, and it will be said: This was for such-and-such, and he did therein such-and-such. No one narrated this hadith from Atiyyah, from Abi Hurayrah, except Amr ibn Atiyyah; Abdullah ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it, and the people narrated it from Atiyyah, from Abi Said al-Khudri."
"5637","5631 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying over funerals among the graves. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Hafs; Husayn ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"5638","5632 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl, that they asked Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa about tayammum. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that it be done like this: he struck the earth with his hands, then shook them off, and wiped his face and his hands. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"5639","5633 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Razin, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabrah, meaning Aba Khaythamah, that his father asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is recited in witr? He said: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High in the first, and: Say, O disbelievers in the second, and: Say, He is Allah, One in the third. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Razin except Yunus ibn Bukayr."
"5640","5634 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Yahya al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb and Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the Turks as long as they leave you, for those who will strip my ummah of what Allah granted them are the Banu Qantura. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Marwan ibn Salim; Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"5641","5635 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ubayd al-Nahhas narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shimr, from al-Amash, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending against injustice is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Amr ibn Shimr; Ubayd al-Nahhas is alone in transmitting it."
"5642","5636 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abi Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, and when morning came he would pray witr with one, and said: Allah is One and loves the odd number. No one narrated this hadith from Atiyyah, from Abi Said, except al-Wassafi, and it is not narrated from Abi Said except with this chain; and al-Amash and Misar and others narrated it from Ibn Umar."
"5643","5637 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abi Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me three stones; then he performed ablution without touching water. He said: Throw away the dung, for it is filth. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, except Abu Sinan; al-Sabbah ibn Muharib is alone in transmitting it."
"5644","5638 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas used to wear silk, and when asked about it, he said: Only pure silk was forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Dinar except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb; Muslim ibn Sallam is alone in transmitting it."
"5645","5639 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abi Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to love the poor and sit with them, to look to one below me and not look to one above me, and to join my kinship even if it turns away."
"5646","5640 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Idris, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a standing, informing us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection; whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Khalid al-Wasiti; and the people of Hijaz and Ibrahim ibn Tahman call him Abbad ibn Ishaq."
"5647","5641 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ziyad al-Susi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Ismail al-Harrani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj and Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abi Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Visit occasionally and love will increase. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Mansur ibn Ismail."
"5648","5642 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hubaysh ibn Mubashshir narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry, and married her. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Yunus al-Muaddib is alone in transmitting it."
"5649","5643 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity early, for calamity does not pass beyond it. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"5650","5644 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abi Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except al-Darawardi; Harb ibn al-Hasan is alone in transmitting it."
"5651","5645 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Duri al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When this verse was revealed: The example of those who spend their wealth in the path of Allah is like a grain that grows seven ears, in every ear a hundred grains, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Lord, increase my ummah. Then was revealed: Who is it that lends Allah a good loan so He multiplies it for him many times. He said: O Lord, increase my ummah. Then was revealed: Only the patient will be paid their reward without measure. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Isa ibn al-Musayyab, nor from Isa except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib; Hafs ibn Umar al-Duri is alone in transmitting it."
"5652","5646 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Sakan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Aws Abu Zayd al-Nahwi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Abi Qatadah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the day of Arafah is expiation for two years: a past year and a coming year, and fasting Ashura is expiation for a year. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Abi Qatadah, except Qays ibn al-Rabi; Abu Zayd al-Nahwi is alone in transmitting it, and the people narrated it from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abi al-Khalil, from Abi Qatadah."
"5653","5647 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Harun al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Salih, from Abi Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while committing it as a believer, nor does he drink wine while drinking it as a believer, but the door of repentance is open. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Sad except Abd al-Rahim ibn Harun."
"5654","5648 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Saluli al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your men among the people of Paradise? The Prophet is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the man who visits his brother for the sake of Allah in a distant part of town is in Paradise. Shall I not inform you of your women among the people of Paradise? The childbearing loving one who, when she wrongs or is wronged, says: Here is my hand in your hand; I shall not taste sleep until you are pleased. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except al-Sari ibn Ismail, nor from Sari except Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi; Said ibn Khuthaym is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Kab ibn Ujrah except with this chain."
"5655","5649 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi narrated to us, he said: Shuayb al-Anmati narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a believer of one of his distresses, Allah will relieve him of his distresses on the Day of Resurrection; whoever covers a fault of a believer, Allah will cover his fault; and whoever eases the distress of a believer, Allah will ease his distress. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Kab except Layth; Shuayb al-Anmati is alone in transmitting it."
"5656","5650 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Asbat narrated to us, he said: Abdurrahman ibn Abi Hammad al-Muqri narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih and Uthman ibn Ruzayq, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some people who had performed ablution, and he said: 'Woe to the heels from the Fire.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Abdurrahman ibn Abi Hammad; Abu al-Asbat was alone in transmitting it."
"5657","5651 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isa al-Qari narrated to us, he said: Mufaddal ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Amr ibn Sa'd, from Yazid ar-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'My Hawd (Pool) is between Aylah and Makkah.' No one narrated this hadith from Mufaddal ibn Yunus except Musa al-Qari; al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"5658","5652 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah as-Saffar narrated to us, from Hisham ad-Dastawa'i, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have cupping done on the seventeenth, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ad-Dastawa'i except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah; Abdallah ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"5659","5653 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Waqid al-Basri narrated to us, from Hisham ad-Dastawa'i, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the last ten nights of Ramadan began, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fold up his bedding, keep away from women, and make his dinner his suhur. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham ad-Dastawa'i, and none from Hisham except Hafs ibn Waqid; Abdallah ibn al-Hakam was alone in transmitting it."
"5660","5654 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, he said: Tahajjud prayer at night used to please the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Aswad ibn Qays except Qays; Abu Bilal was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Jundub except with this chain."
"5661","5655 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn, he said: Jabir ibn Abdillah came to me while I was in the kuttab (school), and he said: 'Uncover your belly,' so I uncovered my belly and he kissed it, then he said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to convey salam to you.' No one narrated this hadith from Aban ibn Taghlib except Mufaddal ibn Salih; Suwayd ibn Sa'id was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"5662","5656 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Yazid at-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whatever the sea leaves dry while it is alive and then it dies, eat it; whatever the sea casts out alive and then it dies, eat it; and whatever you find dead and floating, do not eat it.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Hafs; al-Husayn ibn Yazid was alone in transmitting it."
"5663","5657 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling a heap of dates whose measure is unknown, and a heap of foodstuff. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad except al-Haytham ibn Humayd; al-Hakam ibn Musa was alone in transmitting it."
"5664","5658 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, Abu Quhafah was brought to him, his head and beard as white as thagham (a white plant); he said: 'Change the grey hair, but avoid black.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Sharik; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"5665","5659 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id at-Tubba'i narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Humran, or from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: Uthman ibn Affan called for water for ablution and performed ablution for prayer, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, and prays and performs the prayer well, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except his son; al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam was alone in transmitting it."
"5666","5660 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from Ubadah ibn as-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would take a tuft of wool from the side of a camel from the spoils and say: 'I have in it only the same as any one of you. Beware of ghulul (stealing from spoils), for it is disgrace upon its doer on the Day of Resurrection. Return the needle, the thread, and what is above that, and strive in Allah's cause against the near and the far, in residence and in travel, for jihad is a gate among the gates of Paradise that saves its doer from worry and grief.' No one narrated this hadith from Rabi'ah ibn Najid except Abu Sadiq, and none from Abu Sadiq except al-Qasim ibn al-Walid; Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad was alone in transmitting it."
"5667","5661 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Imran ath-Tha'labi narrated to us, he said: Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far ar-Razi, from ar-Rabi' ibn Anas, he said: The lowest heaven is a restrained wave, the second is rock, the third is iron, the fourth is copper, the fifth is silver, the sixth is gold, and the seventh is ruby. This hadith is not narrated from ar-Rabi' ibn Anas except with this chain; Hakkam ibn Salm was alone in transmitting it."
"5668","5662 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Uthman as-Sari narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf al-Makki narrated to us, from Salim ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the son of Abdallah ibn Ubayy - his father said to him: 'My son, seek a garment from the garments of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and shroud me in it, and ask him to pray over me.' So he came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you know the honour of Abdallah, and he asks you for a garment from your garments to be shrouded in, and that you pray over him.' He said: So he gave him a garment from his garments and intended to pray over him, but Umar ibn al-Khattab said to him: 'Do you not know Abdallah and his hypocrisy? You pray over him while Allah has forbidden you to pray over him?' He said: 'Where?' He said: 'Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.' He said: 'I shall increase over seventy.' Then Allah revealed: 'And do not ever pray over any one of them who dies, nor stand by his grave.' He said: And Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'It is the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them' - the verse. He said: And a man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prolonged his sitting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out three times so that he would get up and follow him, but he did not do so. Then Umar entered, saw the man, and recognized in the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dislike of his sitting, so he said: 'Perhaps you have harmed the Prophet, peace be upon him.' The man understood and stood up, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I stood up three times so that he would follow me, but he did not.' Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would adopt a veil, for your wives are not like other women, and that is purer for their hearts.' Then Allah revealed: 'O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you for a meal, without waiting for its preparation' - the verse. So he sent to Umar and informed him of that. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about the captives of Badr. Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, be considerate toward your people, take the ransom and seek help through it.' Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, kill them.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If you two agreed, you would not be disobeyed.' Then he took the view of Abu Bakr, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has thoroughly subdued in the land.' He said: And when: 'And We created man from an essence of clay, then We made him a drop in a firm lodging' - the verse - was revealed, Umar said: 'Blessed is Allah, the Best of creators,' and there was revealed: 'So blessed is Allah, the Best of creators.' No one narrated this hadith from Salim ibn Ajlan al-Aftas except Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf; Bishr ibn as-Sari was alone in transmitting it."
"5669","5663 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: as-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'I obtained from a woman what is short of intercourse.' Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night' - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except Abdallah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz; as-Sabbah ibn Muharib was alone in transmitting it."
"5670","5664 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Jabir al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were gathered, and he said: 'O company of Muslims, fear Allah and join your ties of kinship, for there is no reward quicker than the reward of joining kinship. Beware of transgression, for there is no punishment quicker than the punishment of transgression. Beware of disobedience to parents, for the fragrance of Paradise is found from a distance of a thousand years, and by Allah, neither a disobedient child, nor one who severs kinship, nor an old adulterer, nor one who drags his garment in pride will find it. Pride belongs only to Allah, Lord of the worlds. All lying is sin except what benefits a believer thereby or wards off thereby something against religion. In Paradise there is a market wherein nothing is sold or bought; there are only images in it, so whoever loves an image of a man or a woman enters into it.' This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Tarif was alone in transmitting it."
"5671","5665 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Bakka'i narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from Abu az-Zinad, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as a man is in the aid of his brother.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu az-Zinad except Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi'; Ubaydullah ibn Musa was alone in transmitting it."
"5672","5666 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Firas Abu Hurayrah as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Awwam - meaning Imran al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdillah ibn ash-Shikhkhir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'The likeness of the son of Adam, with ninety-nine deaths beside him: if the deaths miss him, he falls into old age until he dies.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan and al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj; Abu Qutaybah was alone in transmitting it from Imran, and Ibrahim ibn Tahman was alone in transmitting it from al-Hajjaj, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5673","5667 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdirrahman al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu Abdillah al-Jasri, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah dislikes three things for you: idle talk, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan; Salm ibn Qutaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"5674","5668 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'You hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you.' This hadith is not narrated from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Imran was alone in transmitting it."
"5675","5669 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalaf at-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abdilhamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than the trial of women.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Mindal; Ali ibn Abdilhamid was alone in transmitting it."
"5676","5670 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub Abu Bahz ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas - I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that he said: 'Two greedy ones whose greed is never satisfied: one greedy in seeking knowledge whose greed is never satisfied, and one greedy in seeking the world whose greed is never satisfied.' No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Jarir; Abu Bahz ar-Razi was alone in transmitting it."
"5677","5671 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from ash-Sha'bi, from ad-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah, concerning Allah's saying: 'And do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction, and do good; indeed Allah loves the doers of good.' He said: The Ansar used to give and spend in charity, then a year of hardship struck them and they withheld, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'And do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction, and do good; indeed Allah loves the doers of good.' No one narrates this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Hammad ibn Salamah; Hudbah ibn Khalid was alone in transmitting it. And he said: ad-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah, and the correct is: Abu Jubayrah ibn ad-Dahhak."
"5678","5672 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from an-Nu'man ibn Bashir, concerning Allah the Mighty and Majestic's saying: 'And do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction.' He said: A man would commit a sin and say: 'I will not be forgiven,' so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'And do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction, and do good; indeed Allah loves the doers of good.' No one narrated this hadith from Simak ibn Harb except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"5679","5673 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise, and there is nothing on earth from Paradise except it. It was white like al-maha (white antelope), and were it not for what touched it of the filth of ignorance, no diseased person it touched would fail to be healed.' No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Abi Rabah except Ibn Abi Layla; Muhammad ibn Imran was alone in transmitting it from his father."
"5680","5674 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: I prayed Maghrib behind Ibn az-Zubayr; he gave salam after two rak'ahs, then stood, touched the Stone, and they glorified Allah at him (to alert him), so he returned, completed what remained, and prostrated twice. I came to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that, and he said: 'By his father, he did not deviate from the sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"5681","5675 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Su'ayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Hasan, from his mother, from his grandmother - meaning Fatimah - she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque he would say: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy,' and when he went out he would say the like of that, and he said: 'O Allah, open for me the doors of Your bounty.' No one narrated this hadith from Su'ayr ibn al-Khums except Ibrahim ibn Yusuf."
"5682","5676 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ziyad as-Susi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Sa'id ibn Jumhan, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, if water were poured on his back it would remain settled. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar al-Himsi; Salih ibn Ziyad was alone in transmitting it."
"5683","5677 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'ishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with nine rak'ahs, until when he put on flesh he prayed witr with seven while sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah except Ubays ibn Maymun; Khalaf ibn Hisham was alone in transmitting it."
"5684","5678 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi ar-Rabi' as-Samman narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdallah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in witr: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' and: 'Say: O disbelievers,' and: 'Say: He is Allah, the One.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan."
"5685","5679 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Huraym ibn Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Friday prayer is obligatory upon every adult, except a slave, or a sick person, or a woman, or a child.' This hadith is not narrated from Tariq except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"5686","5680 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Burdah ad-Duhni narrated to us, he said: Abdilkarim ibn Hilal al-Khulqani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah he circumambulated seven times, then turned to the Maqam and prayed two rak'ahs, then turned to Zamzam and said: 'Draw water; were it not that it would become a sunnah, I would draw with my hand.' A bucket was filled for him, he poured some of it into it, then rinsed his mouth into the bucket, and said: 'Pour it into the well.' Then he turned to the Siqayah and said: 'Give me to drink.' Al-Abbas said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, hands have touched this, there are many flies in it, and we have in the house what is better than it.' He said: 'No, give me to drink from this.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abdilkarim ibn Hilal."
"5687","5681 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdilhamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, from Nusayr ibn Dhu'luq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he could not find means to redeem it until he died. No one narrated this hadith from Nusayr ibn Dhu'luq except Qays; Yahya al-Himmani was alone in transmitting it."
"5688","5682 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in prayer he placed his hand upon his knees. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Ibn Abi Za'idah."
"5689","5683 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ba'jah ibn Abdillah ibn Badr al-Juhani, that his father informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them one day: 'This is the day of Ashura, so fast it.' A man from Banu Amr ibn Awf stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I left my people, some of them fasting and some breaking fast.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Go to them; whoever among them is breaking fast, let him abstain, and whoever is fasting, let him complete his fast.' No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam, and it is not narrated from Abdallah ibn Badr except with this chain."
"5690","5684 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdirrahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim as-Sulami narrated to us, from his father, from az-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man from the Muslims came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery.' He turned away from him until he came to him four times, each time turning away from him. When he had asked him four times, he testified against himself four testimonies. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: 'Are you mad?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Are you married?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Take him and stone him.' No one narrated this hadith jointly from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salamah, except Abdirrahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim; none narrated it from Abdirrahman except his son, none from his son except Yahya ibn Ya'la; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it."
"5691","5685 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abyad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Abu Abdirrahman as-Sulami, from Abdallah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us: when one of you sneezes, let him say: 'All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds.' When he says that, let whoever is with him say: 'May Allah have mercy on you.' When he says that, let him say: 'May Allah forgive me and you.' No one narrates this hadith from Ata except Abyad ibn Aban and al-Mughirah ibn Muslim; Ahmad ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting it from Abyad ibn Aban, and an-Nu'man ibn Abdissalam was alone in transmitting it from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim."
"5692","5686 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Shababah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ibrahim as-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Qirtas narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Sulay' narrated to me, he said: I heard A'ishah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'How many a disheveled one in two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfil it - among them is Ammar ibn Yasir.' This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; Isa ibn Qirtas was alone in transmitting it, and none narrated it from Isa ibn Qirtas except Yahya ibn Ibrahim as-Sulami."
"5693","5687 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from ash-Sha'bi, from Jabir, he said: They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, describe your Lord to us.' Then there was revealed: 'Say: He is Allah, the One' to its end. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except his son Isma'il; Surayj ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"5694","5688 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bakkar al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ibn Ashwa', from Abu Layla, freedman of the Ansar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'I have indeed intended to command the prayer to be established, then look at who does not attend the prayer and burn his house over him.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ashwa' except Layth, and none from Layth except Abu Ishaq al-Fazari."
"5695","5689 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Talhah ibn Yazid, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night; he performed ablution and stood praying. I came to him and stood on his left, so he placed me on his right, then he said takbir and said: 'Glory be to Allah, Lord of sovereignty, might, pride, and greatness.' No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far al-Ahmar except Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri."
"5696","5690 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from A'ishah, she said: I used to rub it - meaning semen - from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would pray in it. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, and none from Ja'far except Mindal; Awn ibn Sallam was alone in transmitting it."
"5697","5691 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abdirrahman at-Tara'ifi narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out in summer would go out on Thursday night, and when winter came he would enter on Thursday night. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar ibn Musa, and none from Umar except Uthman ibn Abdirrahman; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"5698","5692 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Awn al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Truffles are from manna, their water is a cure for the eye, and ajwah dates are from Paradise and are a cure for poison.' No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi; Hamzah ibn Awn was alone in transmitting it."
"5699","5693 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three days, except over a husband.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan; Muhammad ibn Bilal was alone in transmitting it."
"5700","5694 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abdilawwal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il, from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Yazid ad-Duba'i, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Hajj in Allah's cause: spending in it, a dirham equals seven hundred.' Thus Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il narrated this hadith from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Yazid ad-Duba'i, from Anas ibn Malik. And Ata ibn as-Sa'ib narrated it from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father. None narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il except Muhammad ibn Bishr; Husayn ibn Abdilawwal was alone in transmitting it."
"5701","5695 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Abdilmalik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abdallah ibn Abdillah ar-Razi, from Yahya ibn Abi Muhammad, from Abu Abdirrahman - the guardian of A'ishah - he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A'ishah praying in a single garment, half of it upon the Prophet, peace be upon him, and half upon A'ishah. No one narrated this hadith from Abdilmalik ibn Abi Sulayman except Ali ibn Hashim; Dirar ibn Surad was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Abdirrahman except with this chain."
"5702","5696 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdilhamid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would extend his head to me while he was in i'tikaf, and I would wash it while I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Muhammad ibn Aban; Abdilhamid ibn Salih was alone in transmitting it."
"5703","5697 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdallah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, he said: al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing and said: 'Allah hears whoever praises Him,' we would not prostrate until we saw him on the ground. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar except Hafs; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr was alone in transmitting it."
"5704","5698 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abdilaziz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi', he said: I saw Ibn Umar, when a man beside him sneezed and said: 'All praise is due to Allah, and peace upon the Messenger of Allah,' Ibn Umar said: 'And I too say: peace upon the Messenger of Allah, but this is not how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to say when we sneeze: All praise is due to Allah in every circumstance.' No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abdilaziz except al-Walid ibn Muslim; Suhayl ibn Salih was alone in transmitting it."
"5705","5699 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Sabbah ibn Yahya al-Muzani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a group from Banu Hashim - or: youths from Banu Hashim - came forward. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them, his face reddened and his eyes filled with tears. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we continually see in your face something you dislike.' He said: 'We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and these members of my household after me will meet expulsion and dispersal, until a people come from here, from the east, bearers of black banners. They will ask for justice and it will not be given to them, then they will ask for justice and it will not be given to them - he said that two or three times - then they will fight and be given what they ask, but they will not accept it until they hand it to a man from my household, who will fill it with justice as they filled it with injustice. Whoever reaches that time, let him come to them even crawling upon snow.' No one narrated this hadith from Sabbah al-Muzani except Abu Ahmad; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"5706","5700 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would follow every prayer with two rak'ahs, except the dawn prayer, for which he would perform them before it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu ad-Duha except Habib ibn Hassan; Abu Ahmad was alone in transmitting it."
"5707","5701 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Atiyyah, from A'ishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hasten the Maghrib prayer and break fast when the sun set. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Umayr except Habib ibn Hassan; Abu Ahmad was alone in transmitting it."
"5708","5702 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kahmas narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Fold your garments, their spirits return to them, for when Satan finds a garment folded he does not wear it, and when he finds it spread out he wears it.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu az-Zubayr except Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5709","5703 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abdirrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): concerning images, he permitted what is trodden upon and disliked what is set up. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Sulayman ibn Arqam."
"5710","5704 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Maysarah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu ad-Darda, he said: Flour was never sifted for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had only a single shirt. This hadith is not narrated from Abu ad-Darda except with this chain; Yunus ibn Bukayr was alone in transmitting it."
"5711","5705 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry.'"
"5712","5706 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ishaq as-Samarqandi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa as-Sinani narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Arafat supplicating; he raised his hands and the camel's halter fell, so he picked it up while keeping his hands raised. The Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: 'This is earnest supplication and humility.'"
"5713","5707 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Musa at-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from az-Zuhri, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while he was in Madinah: 'O Allah, place in it twice the blessing that is in Makkah.' No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Usamah ibn Zayd; Abdallah ibn Musa at-Taymi was alone in transmitting it."
"5714","5708 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever learns knowledge to boast thereby before scholars, or to argue thereby with fools, or to turn thereby the faces of people toward himself, he is in the Fire.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Shayban; Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Wasiti was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"5715","5709 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Abdissalam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, from Salamah ibn Abi Salamah ibn Abdirrahman, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The major sins are seven: associating partners with Allah, killing the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, slandering the chaste woman, fleeing from battle, consuming usury, consuming the orphan's wealth, and returning to Bedouin life after emigration.' This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain; Abu Bilal was alone in transmitting it."
"5716","5710 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Jud'ani narrated to us, he said: Tamim ibn Imran al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Makki, from Fudayl ibn Iyad, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Overlook the fault of the generous, for Allah takes his hand whenever he stumbles.' This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Jud'ani was alone in transmitting it."
"5717","5711 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Kaysi al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: No one of Banu Umayyah rules a year except the children of al-Abbas rule two years. A man from his companions said to him: 'O Abu Hamzah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it?' He said: 'Yes, it is as certain as you being here.' This hadith is not narrated from Anas ibn Malik except with this chain; Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr was alone in transmitting it."
"5718","5712 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from as-Sari ibn Isma'il, from ash-Sha'bi, he said: I heard an-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressing us upon the pulpit of Kufah when Mu'awiyah appointed him over us, saying: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'O people, from grapes comes wine, from raisins comes wine, from dates comes wine, from honey comes wine, and I forbid every intoxicant.' No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and none from Muhammad except Muhammad ibn Salamah; Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harrani was alone in transmitting it."
"5719","5713 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ash-Shami narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not lodge them (women) in upper rooms, do not teach them writing, teach them spinning and Surah an-Nur.' No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"5720","5714 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdilhamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdallah, he said: The number of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr was three hundred. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none from Hammad except Abu Dawud; al-Himmani was alone in transmitting it."
"5721","5715 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, raised (to the Prophet): 'Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Sharik."
"5722","5716 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abdilawwal narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, Ali ibn Zayd, Yunus ibn Ubayd, and Humayd at-Tawil, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There is no Muslim whose three children die but Allah admits them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy.' No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd and Abu Imran al-Jawni except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none from Hammad except Amr ibn Asim; al-Husayn ibn Abdilawwal was alone in transmitting it."
"5723","5717 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Lani narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: Aqil and Talib inherited Abu Talib, and Ali did not inherit him. Ali said: For that reason we left our share in the Shi'b (valley). No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Mu'afa ibn Imran."
"5724","5718 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Ghalib ibn Ubaydillah, Sufyan, and Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Salih, freedman of at-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other.' No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abdilmalik ibn Abi Karimah; Ali ibn Bahram was alone in transmitting it."
"5725","5719 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Abd narrated to us, from Abdilkarim al-Jazari, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he looked at the Ka'bah and said: 'Allah has honoured you, ennobled you, and magnified you, yet the believer is greater in sanctity than you.'"
"5726","5720 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Awf al-A'rabi, from Sulayman ibn Jabir, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Learn the Qur'an and teach it to people, learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to people, for I shall be taken, and soon two men will differ over an inheritance law and find no one to decide between them.' No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Awdi."
"5727","5721 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Habib - meaning Ibn Abi Thabit - from Ziyad ibn Hudayr, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no staying up at night except for one praying or travelling.' No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi."
"5728","5722 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdirrahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Yahya at-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No servant ever puts on sandals, or light shoes, or wears a garment to go out seeking knowledge, but Allah forgives his sins where he steps upon the threshold of his door.' This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Yahya at-Taymi was alone in transmitting it."
"5729","5723 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin except Abu Hilal; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"5730","5724 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: Some cloaks came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he distributed them among his Companions. My father Makhramah said to me: 'Take us to him; perhaps he will give us something of them.' He stopped at the door and said: 'Here he is.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice and came out to him with a cloak in hand; it is as if I am looking at him showing my father the beauties of the cloak, saying: 'I hid this for you.' Salih ibn Hatim said: I said to my father: 'Why did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do this with Makhramah?' He said: 'As if to guard against his tongue.' No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hatim ibn Wardan."
"5731","5725 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hakim al-Azdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Forbidden to the Fire is every gentle, mild, easy, approachable one.' No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Wahb ibn Hakim; Jumhur ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"5732","5726 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Hakim al-Khuza'i narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Isa ar-Raqashi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is ill omen?' He said: 'Bad character.' This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; al-Fadl ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"5733","5727 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abdilqays: 'In you are two traits which Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation.' No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Yahya ibn Talhah."
"5734","5728 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdirrahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from as-Sari ibn Isma'il, from ash-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have family, a mother and a father; which of them is most deserving of my joining ties?' He said: 'Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest.' No one narrated this hadith from ash-Sha'bi except as-Sari ibn Isma'il, and it is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain."
"5735","5729 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn Muhriz narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'If I were to take a close friend, I would take Abu Bakr as a close friend.' No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Awdi except Mahbub ibn Muhriz."
"5736","5730 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Say: He is Allah, the One' equals a third of the Qur'an. No one narrated this hadith from Jarir ibn Hazim except Yazid ibn Harun."
"5737","5731 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The most beloved colour to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was green. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Bashir; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir was alone in transmitting it."
"5738","5732 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Fleas were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'They awaken for prayer.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Bashir and Suwayd Abu Hatim, and none narrated it from Sa'id ibn Bashir except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"5739","5733 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Abbad Yahya ibn Abbad al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a Jewish funeral passed by him, so he stood; it was said: 'It is a Jewish funeral?' He said: 'We stood only for our brothers among the angels.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammad ibn Salamah; Yahya ibn Abbad was alone in transmitting it."
"5740","5734 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his deathbed, he commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief, so he stood with the people behind Abu Bakr, wrapped in a garment."
"5741","5735 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Talut narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When you judge, be just; when you kill, do it well, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic is Good and loves goodness.' No one narrated these two hadiths from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan; Muhammad ibn Bilal was alone in transmitting them."
"5742","5736 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When Ruqayyah, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, he said: 'Join our righteous predecessor, Uthman ibn Maz'un.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Salih al-Murri; Yunus ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"5743","5737 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood (in prayer) until his feet swelled. It was said to him: 'Has Allah not forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what will come later?' He said: 'Should I not be a grateful servant?' No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar, from Qatadah, from Anas, except Abdallah ibn Awn from Muhammad ibn Bishr. Others narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Mis'ar, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. Abu Qatadah al-Harrani narrated it from Mis'ar, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah. Sayf ibn Muhammad, nephew of Sufyan, narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"5744","5738 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from his book, dictating, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Abdirrahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We would perform ablution (again) from a leper when we touched him. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr was alone in transmitting it, and we did not write it except from al-Hadrami; Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal wrote it from him."
"5745","5739 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdilhamid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya al-Qattat except Muhammad ibn Aban; Abdilhamid ibn Salih was alone in transmitting it."
"5746","5740 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ziyad as-Susi narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if a cloud intervenes, complete thirty.' No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Abu al-Ahwas, and none from Abu al-Ahwas except Khalaf ibn Tamim; Salih ibn Ziyad was alone in transmitting it."
"5747","5741 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad az-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not hold back from anything, for I do not permit except what Allah has permitted in His Book, and I do not forbid except what Allah has forbidden in His Book.' No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Ali ibn Asim; az-Za'farani was alone in transmitting it."
"5748","5742 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Jahdar ibn Abdillah ar-Rahabi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'In Paradise there is a house called the House of Generosity.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Baqiyyah; Jahdar ibn Abdillah ar-Rahabi was alone in transmitting it."
"5749","5743 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Jandal ibn Waliq ibn Hijris at-Taghlibi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Umm Salamah with dates and clarified butter. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Sharik."
"5750","5744 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn az-Zubayr al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from ash-Sha'bi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a camel from me, exempting its use for riding until Madinah. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Sharik; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan at-Tall was alone in transmitting it."
"5751","5745 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abdilazim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever among you has no farat (a child who died before him) will not enter Paradise except sparingly.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, not all of us have a farat.' He said: 'Is it not among the farat of one of you that he loses his Muslim brother?'"
"5752","5746 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abdilazim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Marry, for I shall vie with the nations through you. The miscarried foetus will be seen pressing at the gate of Paradise; it will be said to him: Enter. He will say: Not until my parents enter.' These two hadiths are not narrated from Sahl ibn Hunayf except with this chain; Abdilazim ibn Habib was alone in transmitting them."
"5753","5747 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Mardanbah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan as-Suddi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: I heated water in the sun and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ablution, and he said: 'O A'ishah, do not do this, for this causes whiteness (leprosy).' No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Muhammad ibn Marwan, and it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"5754","5748 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abdilkarim ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Abdallah ibn Amr saying one day among a gathering of Muslims including Ibn Umar: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make His creation hear of him on the Day of Resurrection, and belittle him and disgrace him.' Then I saw the eyes of Ibn Umar shedding tears. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Abdilkarim ibn Malik; Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud was alone in transmitting it."
"5755","5749 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Musa al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Mirdas, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim, peace be upon him, said: 'He was named al-Khadir only because he stood upon a white fleece of earth, and it shook forth green.' No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Bilal ibn Mirdas; al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr was alone in transmitting it."
"5756","5750 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abdillah ibn Zurarah ar-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from ash-Sha'bi, from Abu Thabit - and he is Ya'la ibn Murrah - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever steals a handspan of land, or misappropriates it, will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it to the lowest of the earths.' No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qurrah, except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"5757","5751 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Adam al-Basri narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'alla ibn Turkah Abu Abdissamad narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to dispatch an expedition he would send it off early in the morning, saying: 'O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Mas'udi; al-Mu'alla ibn Turkah was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except with this chain."
"5758","5752 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdallah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I have indeed intended to command Bilal to establish the prayer, then turn to a people who heard the call and did not answer, and burn their houses over them.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"5759","5753 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abdillah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-A'sha narrated to us, from Muhill ibn Muhriz ad-Dabbi, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever has a child die - male or female, whether it uttered Islam or not, whether he is content or not, whether he is patient or not - he has no reward but Paradise.' This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain; Amr al-Awdi was alone in transmitting it."
"5760","5754 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mahfuz ibn Bahr al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abdilwahid at-Tamimi narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Ata ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Three are destructive, three are saving, three are expiations, and three are degrees. As for the destructive: obeyed miserliness, followed desire, and a man's admiration of himself. As for the saving: justice in anger and contentment, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of Allah in secret and in public. As for the expiations: waiting for prayer after prayer, performing ablution fully in cold, and moving feet to congregations. As for the degrees: feeding food, spreading salam, and prayer at night while people sleep.' No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except Ata ibn Dinar, and none from Ata except Ibn Lahi'ah; al-Walid ibn Abdilwahid was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"5761","5755 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas ibn Malik, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not say Surah al-Baqarah, nor Surah Al Imran, nor Surah an-Nisa, and likewise the whole Qur'an; rather say: the surah in which the cow is mentioned, the surah in which the family of Imran is mentioned, and thus the whole Qur'an.' No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Anas except Ubays ibn Maymun; Khalaf ibn Hisham was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"5762","5756 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Yahya ibn ar-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from his father Atiyyah, he said: Abdallah ibn Buraydah narrated to me that his father narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali ibn Abi Talib and Khalid ibn al-Walid, saying: 'If there is fighting, Ali is in command over you.' They were given victory and took captives; Ali took a beautiful slave girl to send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but Khalid refused him, saying: 'I shall send her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' When he prevented him, Khalid set out and sent Buraydah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Buraydah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was washing his head, and I spoke against Ali before him - and when we sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would not raise our eyes to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Hush, O Buraydah.' I raised my head to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his face had changed. When I saw that I said: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger.' Buraydah said: By Allah, I shall never hate him after what I saw from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Atiyyah except his son Amr."
"5763","5757 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Yahya ibn ar-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his father Atiyyah, he said: Abdallah ibn Buraydah narrated to me that Buraydah narrated to him that he witnessed the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'No man is placed in command over ten or more but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck: if he was good it will be released from him, and if he was bad, chains will be added to his chains.' No one narrated this hadith from Atiyyah except his son Amr and Isa ibn al-Musayyib."
"5764","5758 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Nusayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Uthman Abu al-Yaqzan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Ansar said among themselves: 'If only we collected wealth for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), extending his hand freely with none coming between him and it?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we wish to collect for you from our wealth.' Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'Say: I ask you no reward for it except love for kin.' They went out differing; they said: 'Have you not seen what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said?' Some of them said: 'He said this only that we may fight for his household and support them.' Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: 'Or do they say: He has forged a lie against Allah' up to His saying: 'And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants.' He held out repentance to them, up to His saying: 'And those who believe and do righteous deeds respond, and He increases them of His bounty' - they are those who said this, that they repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman Abu al-Yaqzan except Nusayr ibn Ziyad; Husayn al-Ashqar was alone in transmitting it."
"5765","5759 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Nafi' al-Ash'ari narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.' No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah except Khalid ibn Nafi'."
"5766","5760 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ubayd at-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of donkeys and commanded that horse meat be eaten. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir ibn Zayd except Simak, and none from Simak except Umar ibn Ubayd; Muhammad ibn Ubayd was alone in transmitting it."
"5767","5761 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from ash-Sha'bi, that Abdallah ibn Abbas used to say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Lord twice: once with his sight and once with his heart. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except his son Isma'il."
"5768","5762 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Sayf, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdallah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I asked my Lord that I not marry into anyone nor give in marriage to anyone but that he be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that.' No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Ammar ibn Sayf, and none from Ammar except Qabisah; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"5769","5763 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdilhamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sharhabil al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Isa, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Would it please you to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?' They said takbir. Then he said: 'Would it please you to be a third of the people of Paradise?' They said takbir. Then he said: 'Would it please you to be half of the people of Paradise?' They said takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'People on the Day of Resurrection will be one hundred and twenty rows; my nation among them will be eighty rows.' No one narrated this hadith from Abdallah ibn Isa except Muhammad ibn Sharhabil; Yahya al-Himmani was alone in transmitting it."
"5770","5764 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdilhamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Isa, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Learn al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the batalah (sorcerers / the idle) cannot bear it.' And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The Qur'an will come on the Day of Resurrection like a pale man, saying to its companion: Do you know me? I am the one who kept your night wakeful and made your midday thirsty. Every trader is behind his trade, and I am for you today beyond every trader. He will be given dominion in his right hand and eternity in his left, a crown of dignity will be placed upon his head, and his parents will be clothed in two garments for which the world and what is in it cannot stand. They will say: O Lord, how is this for us? It will be said to them: For teaching your child the Qur'an. The companion of the Qur'an will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Recite and ascend through the ranks, and chant as you used to chant in the world, for your station is at the last verse with you.' No one narrated this hadith from Abdallah ibn Isa except Sharik, and none narrated it from Sharik except Yazid ibn Harun and Yahya al-Himmani."
"5771","5765 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Paradise has one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is a distance of five hundred years.' No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Sharik."
"5772","5766 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Abu Burdah narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A lahd (niche grave) was dug for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), bricks were set over it upright, and soil was taken from the direction of the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Abu Burdah."
"5773","5767 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdallah, he said: I cannot count how often I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the two rak'ahs after Maghrib and the two before Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan and al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"5774","5768 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi ar-Rabi' as-Samman narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, from Zirr and Abu Wa'il, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, he said: It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), giving salam to his right: 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,' and to his left: 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim, from Zirr, except Abdilmalik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan."
"5775","5769 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Awn al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to supplicate with these supplications at the beginning of his speech, and with them he would seal: 'O Allah, set right relations among us, guide us to the paths of peace, bring us out from darknesses into light, turn away from us indecency, what is apparent of it and what is hidden, bless for us our hearing, our sight, our spouses, our offspring, and our livelihoods, and turn to us in forgiveness; indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful. O Allah, make us grateful for Your blessings, praising thereby, accepting them.' No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Awdi except al-Walid ibn al-Qasim."
"5776","5770 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdiljabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Isma'il al-Kindi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdallah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning His, the Mighty and Majestic's, saying: 'He will pay them their rewards in full and increase them of His bounty' - (that is) intercession for those for whom the Fire became due, among those to whom kindness was done in the world. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Isma'il al-Kindi; Baqiyyah was alone in transmitting it."
"5777","5771 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Suqayr narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a Bedouin man: 'When a desire or a fear befalls you, to whom do you turn?' They said: 'To Allah.' He said: 'When He answers you, to whom do you return?' They said: 'To what you know.' He said: 'You know and do not act, and you act and do not know' - three times. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none from Hammad except Mansur ibn Suqayr."
"5778","5772 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Hiql; Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harbi was alone in transmitting it."
"5779","5773 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, and from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No believer is pricked by a thorn or more but Allah removes thereby a sin from him and raises him thereby a degree.' No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri."
"5780","5774 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna Abu Hatim al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Ayzar narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Overlook the slips of the honourable.'"
"5781","5775 - And with his chain he said: 'Give gifts, you will increase in love.' No one narrated these two hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn al-Ayzar except al-Muthanna Abu Hatim, and none narrated them from al-Muthanna except Muhammad ibn Abi Dawud and Rayhan ibn Sa'id."
"5782","5776 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Firdaws ibn al-Ash'ari narrated to us, from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Mulaykah, from az-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, that Abdirrahman ibn Awf came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having dyed with yellow, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'What is this dye - have you married?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you give a feast?' He said: 'No.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw to him a gold date-stone's weight of gold, saying: 'Give a feast even with a sheep.' No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Abdirrahman al-Mulayki, and none narrated it from Abdirrahman except Firdaws; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it."
"5783","5777 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq as-Sini narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he would place nothing under his feet, except that one day it rained upon us, so he placed a leather mat under his feet. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh except Qays; Ibrahim as-Sini was alone in transmitting it."
"5784","5778 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdallah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: 'What is wealth?' He said: 'Despair of what is in people's hands.' No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ibrahim ibn Ziyad was alone in transmitting it."
"5785","5779 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abdillah al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Two eyes shall not see the Fire: an eye that wept out of awe from fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night guarding in Allah's cause.' No one narrates this hadith from Shabib ibn Bishr except Isra'il; Zafir ibn Sulayman was alone in transmitting it."
"5786","5780 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Umari, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Remember often the destroyer of pleasures - meaning death - for it was never in abundance but it diminished it, nor in little but it sufficed it.' No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abu Amir al-Asadi; Minjab was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"5787","5781 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to sleep among people, and to sleep on the middle of the road. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Abu Bilal was alone in transmitting it."
"5788","5782 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah hates a seventy-year-old in the appearance of a twenty-year-old, in his walk and his look.' This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"5789","5783 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Burd ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Saffanah an-Nakha'i, from A'ishah, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Abu Saffanah except Burd ibn Abi Ziyad; Abthar ibn al-Qasim was alone in transmitting it."
"5790","5784 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb an-Nasha'i al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Khut narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fasts Ramadan, goes to the prayer place with a bath, and seals it with charity, returns forgiven.' No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ayyub ibn Khut; Nasr ibn Hammad was alone in transmitting it."
"5791","5785 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Harith al-Warraq Nasr ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Abdillah al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever recites: Say: He is Allah, the One, in the illness in which he dies, will not be tried in his grave, will be safe from the squeezing of the grave, and the angels will carry him on the Day of Resurrection upon their palms until they pass him over the Sirat to Paradise.' This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Abu al-Harith al-Warraq was alone in transmitting it. And Yazid ibn Abdillah is Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn ash-Shikhkhir."
"5792","5786 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd an-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When one of you prostrates, let him place his palms directly upon the ground; perhaps Allah will release the chains from him on the Day of Resurrection.' No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Dhi'b; Ubayd an-Nahhas was alone in transmitting it."
"5793","5787 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: Abdilmalik ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The believer befriends and is befriended, and there is no good in one who does not befriend nor is befriended; the best of people are the most beneficial to people.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abdilmalik ibn Abi Karimah; Ali ibn Bahram was alone in transmitting it."
"5794","5788 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn al-Husayn Abu al-Hasan as-Saluli narrated to us, he said: as-Subayy ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'For the traveller, three days with their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night' - concerning wiping over the leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except as-Subayy ibn al-Ash'ath; Musa ibn al-Husayn was alone in transmitting it."
"5795","5789 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Abdilmalik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Farwah, from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I shall surely give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love,' and he gave it to Ali. No one narrated this hadith from Abdilmalik ibn Abi Sulayman except Ali ibn Hashim; Dirar ibn Surad was alone in transmitting it."
"5796","5790 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Abi Nasr as-Sakuni narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No servant believes until I am dearer to him than himself, my family dearer to him than his family, my kin dearer to him than his kin, and my self dearer to him than his self.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Ibn Abi Layla, and none from Ibn Abi Layla except Sa'id ibn Amr as-Sakuni."
"5797","5791 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered their mosque and drank while standing. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Sharik."
"5798","5792 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abdissamad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Farqad, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight.' No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar, steward of the family of az-Zubayr, except Umar ibn Farqad; Abdissamad ibn Sulayman was alone in transmitting it, as was Abdissamad ibn Nasr. Umar ibn Farqad is Basran."
"5799","5793 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Farra narrated to us, he said: Ibn Qanbar narrated to us, he said: My father Qanbar narrated to us, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best of my nation are its sharp-tempered ones, who when they become angry return (to calm).' This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Farra was alone in transmitting it."
"5800","5794 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar ibn Bakkar as-Sa'di narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Ibn Sari' at-Tamimi, he said: I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, I have composed poetry in which I praised Allah and praised you.' He said: 'As for what you praised Allah with, bring it; what you praised me with, leave it.' I began reciting to him, then a tall man entered, and he said: 'Hold.' When he went out he said: 'Bring.' I began reciting to him, and before long he returned, saying to me: 'Hold.' When he went out he said to me: 'Bring.' I said: 'Who is this, O Prophet of Allah, that when he enters you say: Hold, and when he goes out you say: Bring?' He said: 'This is Umar, and he is not of falsehood in anything.' No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd; Ma'mar ibn Bakkar was alone in transmitting it."
"5801","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: My love is due for those who give generously to one another for My sake, and My love is due for those who visit one another for My sake. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except Abu Bakr al-Nahshali; Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"5802","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Muhaysin, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) requested Suhayl ibn Amr to bring him some Zamzam water as a gift. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Muhaysin, who is Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin al-Muqri, one of the reciters of the people of Makkah, except Abd Allah ibn Muammil, and no one narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muammil except Hushaym; Sufyan ibn Bishr al-Kufi alone narrated it."
"5803","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fills a gap in a row, Allah raises him a degree thereby and builds for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Maqburi except Ibn Abi Dhib, and no one narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhib except Muslim ibn Khalid; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas alone narrated it."
"5804","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined together both his parents for Sad [as ransom, saying: May my father and mother be ransom for you]. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Husayn al-Jufi; Abd Allah ibn Umar alone narrated it."
"5805","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Faydi narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Nuh narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let your house suffice you, weep over remembrance of your sin, and hold your tongue. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman except al-Masudi, and no one narrated it from al-Masudi except Jabir ibn Nuh; Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Faydi alone narrated it."
"5806","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Isa ibn Mahan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Amir ibn Sad al-Zuhri, from Aishah who said: A woman was divorced at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and waited twenty-three or a little over twenty days, then she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Seek prosperity in your affair, meaning: marry. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Amir ibn Sad, except Abu Jafar al-Razi Isa ibn Mahan; Hatim ibn Ismail alone narrated it."
"5807","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Dirar ibn Surad alone narrated it."
"5808","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Wail ibn Dawud, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When seventy men from among us go to Friday prayer, they are like the seventy of Musa who came as a delegation to their Lord, or better. No one narrated this hadith from Wail ibn Dawud except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri; Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi alone narrated it."
"5809","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Nakhai narrated to us, he said: Sulaym, the freed slave of al-Shabi, narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting after Maghrib with his Companions when a group of travelers passed by him walking, their driver reciting and their guide chanting to the camels; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them he got up hurrying without a cloak, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we will spare you; he said: Leave me to convey to them what was revealed to me concerning their matter. He caught up with them and said: Where are you heading at this hour? They said: We are heading to Yemen. He said: What is this traveling at this hour? Allah has in the heaven a great authority which He directs toward the earth, so do not travel even a step except for what a man finds in his stomach and bladder of urine which he must relieve, then not a step further. As for you, O driver of the people, keep to some of the speech of the Arabs from their rajaz poetry, and when you are riding recite it. And keep to traveling by night, for Allah Almighty has angels entrusted who fold up the earth for the traveler as scrolls are folded. After dawn the people praise the night journey. Let no poet accompany you, nor a soothsayer, nor let a stray beast accompany you, and do not turn away a beggar if you want profit, safety, and good companionship. I wonder how I can sleep when all eyes sleep, for Allah Almighty and His Messenger forbid you from traveling at this hour. No one narrated this hadith from Sulaym, the freed slave of al-Shabi, except Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Nakhai; Ahmad ibn Musarrif alone narrated it."
"5810","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, from his father, from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi, from Yazid ibn Muawiyah al-Bakkai who said: I heard Hudhayfah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, then Allah appointed Abu Bakr as successor, then Abu Bakr passed away and Allah appointed Umar as successor, then Umar passed away and Allah appointed Uthman as successor. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abjar except his son; Abu Usamah alone narrated it."
"5811","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Opening of the Book in the last two rakahs, meaning of Zuhr and Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Sinan ibn Harun; Awn ibn Sallam alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"5812","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abd Allah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange and will return strange, so glad tidings to the strangers. Before the Hour there will be trials like pieces of the dark night; a man will be a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, and a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening; some people will sell their religion for worldly gain. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Jarir; Salih ibn Abd Allah al-Tirmidhi alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"5813","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the alms-collector comes to you, let him not leave except satisfied. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; Muhammad ibn Tarif alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"5814","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Said al-Tubbai narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited the Ansar to grant them land in Bahrain, and they said: No, unless you grant the same to our brothers the Muhajirun. He said: You will see after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me."
"5815","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Tubbai narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A Bedouin came and urinated at the side of the mosque, and the people shouted at him, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restrained them, then ordered a bucket of water to be poured over his urine. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Man except al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani."
"5816","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Sallam, from Said ibn Masruq, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, grief appeared on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then it was lifted from him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw in you what we had not seen. He said: I remembered Zaynab, her weakness, and the pressure of the grave; it has been made easy for her, yet it pressed her with a pressure that reached the horizons. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Masruq except Zakariyya ibn Sallam; Ishaq ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"5817","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Azraq ibn Ali Abu al-Jahm narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah who said: Abd Allah said: I know the paired chapters which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with: al-Dhariyat and al-Tur, and al-Najm, and Iqtarabat, and al-Rahman, and al-Waqiah, and Nun, and al-Haqqah, and Saala Sail, and al-Muzzammil, and La Uqsimu bi-Yawm al-Qiyamah, and Hal Ata ala al-Insan, and al-Mursalat, and Amma Yatasaalun, and al-Naziat, and Abasa, and Wayl lil-Mutaffifin, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except his two sons Muhammad and Yahya; Hassan ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it from Muhammad."
"5818","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Sulayman ibn Urayb, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of a righteous man is glad tidings from Allah, and it is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. I narrated it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is one part of fifty parts of prophethood. This hadith is not narrated from al-Abbas except with this chain; Ali ibn Hakim alone narrated it."
"5819","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mahfuz ibn Bahr al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The banner which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed to Ali was white. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar ibn Musa, and no one narrated it from Umar except al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid; Mahfuz ibn Bahr alone narrated it."
"5820","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Mahfuz ibn Bahr al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: Ubaydah al-Salmani narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself, and I met him with water. He said: Who ordered you to do this? I said: No one ordered me. He said: You have done well; glad tidings of Paradise to you. Then Ali came and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, except Abu Maryam; al-Amash and Abu al-Jahhaf narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Ubaydah, from Abd Allah."
"5821","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Khalid ibn al-Walid who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. This hadith is not narrated from Khalid ibn al-Walid except with this chain; Muqaddam ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"5822","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qaqa ibn Zakariyya al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: We were talking about the day of Uhud while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying; when he finished and turned from his prayer he turned to us and said: Shall I not tell you about the day of Uhud? I saw myself with no one with me except Jibril on my right and Talhah on my left. No one narrated this hadith from Isa ibn Talhah except Talhah ibn Yahya, and no one narrated it from Talhah ibn Yahya except Ibn Idris; al-Qaqa ibn Zakariyya alone narrated it."
"5823","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Ala al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Bahr al-Saqqa, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two groups of my nation will not receive my intercession: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except al-Qasim ibn al-Ala."
"5824","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of a dead person, the one on whose behalf he performed Hajj gets the like of his reward; whoever gives breakfast to a fasting person gets the like of his reward; and whoever guides to good gets the like of the reward of its doer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah; Ali ibn Bahram alone narrated it."
"5825","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Salih, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fulfills the oaths of his parents, pays their debts, and does not cause them to be reviled, is recorded as dutiful even if he was disobedient; and whoever does not fulfill their oaths, does not pay their debts, and causes them to be reviled, is recorded as disobedient even if he was dutiful during their lifetime. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah except with this chain; Hafs ibn Ghiyath alone narrated it."
"5826","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Husayn al-Qantari narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies without an imam over him dies a death of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan alone narrated it, while others besides Shadhan narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim ibn Bahdalah."
"5827","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Sulami Abu al-Hasan al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Muharib ibn Muslim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah: that Jibril, peace be upon him, circumcised the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he purified his heart. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah alone narrated it."
"5828","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabalah al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Numan narrated to us, from Kathir Abu al-Fadl, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: What day is this? We said: The day of sacrifice. He said: What month is this? We said: Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month. He said: What land is this? We said: A sacred land. He said: Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sacredness of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours; let the witness convey to the absent. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar ibn Yasir except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabalah alone narrated it."
"5829","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Zufar narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Said ibn Masruq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: There was nothing on earth more hateful to me than Pharaoh; when he believed with his mouth I began stuffing his mouth with mud, fearing that mercy would reach him."
"5830","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to me, from Nusayr ibn al-Ashath, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Musa who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, forgive me what I have done before and what I do after, what I concealed and what I declared, and what You know better than I; You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, and You have power over all things. No one narrated this hadith from Nusayr ibn al-Ashath except Anbasah; his son alone narrated it from him."
"5831","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Umar, meaning one of Tamim, from Umar: that he kissed the Black Stone and said: I know you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits; were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not kiss you. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Sharik; Abu Bilal alone narrated it."
"5832","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be in my nation a man who speaks after death. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Sharik; Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi alone narrated it."
"5833","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Hiqq narrated to us, from Ibn Awn and Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: Uqbah ibn Amir went out to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad when he was governor over Egypt, and there was an affair between him and the doorkeeper; when he admitted him, he entered upon him and said: Welcome to my brother as a visitor. He said: I did not come to you as a visitor, but for a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5834","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn al-Qadi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is granted a life-grant is his and his descendants. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"5835","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Yahya al-Saidi narrated to us, from Misar, from Simak al-Hanafi, from Ibn Umar who said: It is not a shortening, but it is complete, meaning the two rakahs in travel."
"5836","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Misar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was told that Pharaoh was broken-toothed."
"5837","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Yahya al-Saidi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: I heard Sad saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never joined both his parents together for anyone except me; he said: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you. No one narrated these hadiths from Nuaym ibn Yahya al-Saidi, who is Kufan, trustworthy, rare in hadith, except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5838","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali who said: Umm Salamah said to me: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reviled among you upon the pulpits? I said: Glory be to Allah, how could the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be reviled? She said: Is not Ali ibn Abi Talib and whoever loves him reviled? I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami."
"5839","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibrahim ibn Ismail, and no one narrated it from Ibrahim except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Ubayd ibn Yaish alone narrated it. And the nephew of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from his mother Umm Kulthum."
"5840","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come upon you a man from the best of Dhi Yaman, with the wipe of an angel on his face; then I came. No one narrated this hadith from Qabus except Abu Kudaynah; Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi alone narrated it."
"5841","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was to you like Abu Zara to Umm Zara."
"5842","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, he said: Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out to the prayer place. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Sawwar ibn Musab alone narrated it."
"5843","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade throwing pebbles with fingers, saying: It gouges the eye and breaks the tooth. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Ashath ibn Sawwar; Ali ibn Mushir alone narrated it."
"5844","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieving himself between two mud bricks, facing the qiblah, on top of a house. Ayyub ibn Utbah said: As if it startled him."
"5845","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn Utbah."
"5846","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Misar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both; be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd. This hadith is not narrated from Misar except with this chain."
"5847","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Jarir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave flees, the protection is absolved from him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Sharik."
"5848","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Hujr ibn Adi, from Sharahil ibn Murrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: Rejoice, O Ali, your life and your death are with me. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Qays, and it is not narrated from Sharahil ibn Murrah except with this chain."
"5849","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that when he wanted to touch the Black Stone he would say: O Allah, out of faith in You, belief in Your Book, and the Sunnah of Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would touch it. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Muhammad ibn Muhajir; Awn ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"5850","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, I only know he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is Arafat. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"5851","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Alawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, I think from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: I heard Sad saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Dhib, and no one narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhib except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ahmad ibn Isa al-Alawi alone narrated it."
"5852","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Alawi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, have mercy on my successors. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are your successors? He said: Those who come after me, narrate my hadiths and my Sunnah, and teach them to the people. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sad, and no one narrated it from Hisham except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ahmad ibn Isa al-Alawi alone narrated it."
"5853","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa who said: I entered upon Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan when he had an ulcer on his back and was groaning severely from it. I said: Is all this from this? He said: I would not wish this groaning had not been, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim suffers harm in his body except that it is expiation for his sins, and this is the severest harm. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Yahya except Yunus ibn Bukayr, and no one narrated it from Muawiyah except Abu Burdah."
"5854","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, and from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: As if I am looking at the glimmer of perfume in the partings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was chanting the Talbiyah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, except Zuhayr; the well-known version is the hadith of Ibrahim, from al-Aswad."
"5855","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ashath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his Companions share at al-Hudaybiyah in the sacrificial animals, seven to each."
"5856","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabus ibn Mukhariq, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation is blessed in which the right of the weak is not taken without hesitation. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Sharik."
"5857","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Witr upon his mount. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, and no one narrated it from Yunus except Abd Allah ibn al-Harith; Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"5858","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Bajali al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn al-Urani narrated to us, from Abu Israil al-Mulai, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen? He said: Radiant with white marks from ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Israil except Hasan ibn Husayn."
"5859","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his uncle Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The man who used to backbite people in this world will be brought and told: Eat the flesh of your brother dead as you ate it alive. He will eat it, screaming and grimacing. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Yasar except Ibn Ishaq."
"5860","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said Abu Umar al-Darir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of the people of Hell I have not yet seen: men with whips like the tails of cattle beating people with them, and women clothed yet naked, swaying and causing to sway, with heads like the humps of camels; they will not enter Paradise nor find its fragrance. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah except Zuhayr."
"5861","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man touch another man skin to skin, nor a woman another woman. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin except Hisham, and no one narrated it from Hisham except Abu Bakr; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"5862","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith joined, from Fudayl ibn Iyad, from Ibn Abi Layla and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5863","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abd Allah who said: A rabbi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, or: O Abu al-Qasim, Allah Almighty will hold the heavens on the Day of Resurrection upon a finger, the mountains and trees upon a finger, the water and soil upon a finger, and the rest of creation upon a finger, then He will shake them and say: I am the King, I am the King. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed in wonder at what the rabbi said and confirming him, then recited: And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves, while the earth entirely will be His grip on the Day of Resurrection and the heavens folded in His right hand; glory be to Him, exalted above what they associate. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Ahmad ibn Yunus and Yahya ibn al-Qattan."
"5864","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur and Husayn, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, would rub his mouth with the tooth-stick. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad joined from Husayn and Mansur except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5865","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Nuaym ibn Dajajah who said: Ali said to Abu Masud: Are you the one who says: No hundred years will come upon the people with a blinking eye remaining? He only said: No hundred years will come upon the people with a blinking eye remaining from among those alive today; the relief of this nation and its prosperity is after the hundred. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5866","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The scent of a child is from the scent of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah except Abd al-Majid, and no one narrated it from Abd al-Majid except Mindal ibn Ali."
"5867","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These begging questions are a scratching by which a man scratches his face; whoever wishes keeps his face intact and whoever wishes leaves it, except that a man asks one in authority when he cannot do without him. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5868","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, and he said: Look at which man you see as highest in your eyes. I looked and saw a man wearing a fine suit with people around him; I said: This one. He said: Look at which man you see as lowest in your eyes. I looked and saw a man wearing a cloak; I said: This one. He said: This one is better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the earth full of the like of that one. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5869","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while his armor was pawned with a Jewish man for thirty measures of barley which he took as food for his family. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"5870","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Said ibn Masruq, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ziyad ibn al-Jarrah, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil who said: I heard my father saying to Abd Allah: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Said except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"5871","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Firas, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever acts to be seen, Allah will show him. No one narrated this hadith from Firas except Shayban; Muawiyah ibn Hisham alone narrated it."
"5872","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Hammad Abu al-Harith al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, and there is no prophet after me. No one narrated this hadith [except ...]."
"5873","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi al-Kufi Abu Mulayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever among you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, except al-Walid ibn Uqbah; Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it. And Muawiyah ibn Amr and others narrated it from Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii."
"5874","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), slaughtering two horned white-black rams, placing his foot on their sides, naming Allah and magnifying Him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Musab ibn al-Miqdam."
"5875","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz Abu Mulayl al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Muhammad ibn Aban, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani except al-Walid; Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it. And Muawiyah ibn Amr and others narrated it from his father, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii."
"5876","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Salamah al-Saigh, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The likeness of my household is the likeness of the ark of Nuh; whoever boards it is saved and whoever stays behind drowns. The likeness of my household among you is the likeness of the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israil; whoever enters is forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salamah al-Saigh except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hammad; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah alone narrated it."
"5877","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest: This is what my Lord promised me, then he recited: When the help of Allah comes and the victory. He said: When people entered the religion of Allah in crowds, the religion of Allah prevailed over all religion, so the people are good and we are good. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb; Yahya ibn Adam alone narrated it."
"5878","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespans of my nation are between sixty and seventy; and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest of my nation are the children of seventy. No one narrated this hadith from Kamil ibn al-Ala except Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi."
"5879","And with the same chain: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, Abu al-Umays narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from his father who said: When Ibn Masud died, Abd Allah ibn Masud wept over him, and they said to him: You weep? He said: Yes, my brother in lineage, my companion with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the most beloved of people to me, except for what was from Umar ibn al-Khattab. No one narrated this hadith from Awn ibn Abd Allah except Abu al-Umays."
"5880","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Masruq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri, from Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about monkeys and pigs, and he said: When Allah Almighty is angry with a people, He gives them no progeny nor posterity. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb."
"5881","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Yazid al-Thumali, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will be given their rewards twice: a slave who fulfills the right of Allah made obligatory upon him and the right of his masters, he will be given his reward twice on the Day of Resurrection; a man who had a beautiful slave-girl, disciplined her well, then freed her and married her seeking thereby the face of Allah, he will be given his reward twice; and a man who believed in the first Book, then the latter Book came and he believed in it, he will be given his reward twice."
"5882","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shabi, from Jarir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave joins the land of the enemy, his blood becomes lawful. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii except Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd; his son Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"5883","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her father who died without performing Hajj. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi alone narrated it."
"5884","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Miserliness and faith never combine in the heart of a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Yahya ibn Yaman."
"5885","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, he said: My brother Husayn narrated to me, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Qays; Harun ibn Abi Burdah alone narrated it from his brother."
"5886","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it weighed upon him thereby, and his forehead would sweat profusely like pearls. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman; Yunus ibn Bukayr alone narrated it."
"5887","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail who said: Abd Allah said: I am told of your gathering, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us with admonition on selected days, disliking weariness for us. He said: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah, the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, except Ali ibn Mushir; Minjab ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"5888","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kindi narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and sufficiency. No one narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah except Muhammad ibn Masruq."
"5889","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mahdi al-Attar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever dies in one of the two sanctuaries, Makkah or Madinah, will be raised secure. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil; Zayd ibn al-Hubab alone narrated it."
"5890","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mahdi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Bazigh al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Abu Muadh, from Abu Bishr Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believer except that he has a sin which he commits time after time; the believer is forgetful, and when reminded he remembers. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bishr except Abu Muadh, who is Sulayman ibn Arqam."
"5891","Muhammad ibn Said ibn Duhaym al-Ghamdani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hayyaji narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Subayh al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Uwaym ibn Saidah al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people of Quba: I hear Allah has praised you well for purification, so what is this purification? They said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we know nothing except that our Jewish neighbors, we saw them washing their posteriors after relieving themselves, so we washed as they washed. This hadith is not narrated from Uwaym ibn Saidah except with this chain; Abu Uways alone narrated it."
"5892","Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Abdi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A roasted bird was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said: O Lord, and to me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam except Mufaddal ibn Salih; Muhammad ibn Tarif alone narrated it."
"5893","Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Musab Abu Musab al-Madani, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no charity upon a man for his slave nor his horse, except the charity of Fitr. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Abd al-Salam ibn Musab."
"5894","Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hassan, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes kiss me while he was fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Ali ibn Hashim."
"5895","Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Zafarani narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not delay the Maghrib prayer for Isha nor anything else. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad except Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Zafarani."
"5896","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Ushnani al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali who said: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying; when he finished he said: May Allah curse the scorpion, it spares neither one praying nor anyone else. Then he called for water and salt, began wiping over it, and reciting: Say: O disbelievers, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Ibn Fudayl; Ismail ibn Musa alone narrated it."
"5897","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Ushnani narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of a believer is one part of seventy parts of prophethood. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin except Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr; Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami alone narrated it."
"5898","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Ushnani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Musab narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three days, except for a husband. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Dinar except Abd al-Salam ibn Musab."
"5899","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A person is with whom he loves. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain from the hadith of al-Amash."
"5900","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Waddah al-Tamimi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for me twenty-five times, each time I counted them on my hand. He said: He would say: Have you paid your fathers debt? I would say: Yes. Then he would say: May Allah forgive you. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Shayban; Muawiyah ibn Hisham alone narrated it."
"5901","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Waddah al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Israil, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Yahya ibn Hisham, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched toward Banu Lihyan, placing the Kabah behind him, then said: O Jabir ibn Abd Allah. I came to him, and he sent me for a need of his. I came to him and said: I have come to them and did such and such, but he did not answer me with anything. I returned and said: Perhaps I did not understand the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I returned to him and said: I have come to them and did such and such. He said: I was praying. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Israil; Musab ibn al-Miqdam alone narrated it."
"5902","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir al-Dubai narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah ibn Asma narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I agreed with my Lord in three matters: the veil, the station of Ibrahim, and the captives of Badr. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Juwayriyah; Said ibn Amir alone narrated it."
"5903","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traders, there is no sale between them until they part, except a sale with option. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Said ibn Amir."
"5904","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ulaylah ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for a cupper called Abu Taybah, and he cupped him after Asr in Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ulaylah ibn Badr, who is al-Rabi ibn Badr."
"5905","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Maysarah al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Khalid al-Dalani narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: We used to sell the ornamented sword and buy it with silver. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, and it is not narrated from Tariq except with this chain."
"5906","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to travel from Makkah to Madinah praying two rakahs, two rakahs, fearing none but Allah, blessed and exalted."
"5907","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him his wage; had it been impure he would not have paid him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman except Muslim ibn Ibrahim, Abu Nuaym, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"5908","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The soul of the believer leaves with sweat, and I do not like a death like the death of a donkey. It was said: What is the death of a donkey? He said: Sudden death. He said: And the soul of the disbeliever leaves from its jaws. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Mashar except Husam ibn Misakk; Muslim ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"5909","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Bayan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rijal narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No youth honors an elder for his age except that Allah appoints for him one who will honor him at his age. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Yazid ibn Bayan alone narrated it."
"5910","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your youth are those who resemble your elders, and the worst of your elders are those who resemble your youth."
"5911","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When was your last encounter with Umm Mildam? He said: What is Umm Mildam? He said: Heat between the skin and the bone, sucking blood and eating flesh. He said: I have never complained. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to look at a man of the people of Hell, let him look at this one. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him away from me. No one narrated these two hadiths from Thabit except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar; Muslim ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"5912","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr, he married his daughter to me, carried me to the abode of migration, and bought Bilal with his wealth. May Allah have mercy on Umar, he speaks the truth even if bitter; the truth left him with no friend. May Allah have mercy on Uthman, the angels are shy before him. May Allah have mercy on Ali; O Allah, turn the truth with him wherever he turns. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Abu Attab al-Dallal alone narrated it."
"5913","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married along with her paternal aunt nor her maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam and Said ibn Bashir; Abu Asim alone narrated it from Hammam, and Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi from Said ibn Bashir."
"5914","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: al-Hudhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jummani narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Hudhayl ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"5915","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Anbasah, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Speaking about destiny was delayed for the worst of my nation at the end of time, and disputing about the Quran is disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Anbasah ibn Mahdi al-Haddad."
"5916","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi: that he prayed behind Ibn Abbas over a funeral, and he recited the Opening of the Book aloud, saying: I wanted people to know it is the Sunnah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hammam; al-Hawdi alone narrated it."
"5917","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Shaqiq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, his knees would touch the ground before his palms, and when he rose at the end of two rakahs he would rise upon his knees, leaning on his thighs. No one narrated this hadith from Shaqiq ibn Abi Abd Allah except Hammam."
"5918","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution: rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet three times. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, except Amir al-Ahwal; Hammam alone narrated it."
"5919","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them the prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, mend our relations, and unite our hearts. O Allah, this is Your servant so-and-so son of so-and-so, we know only good, and You know him better, so forgive us and him. I said to him, I being the youngest of the people: If I do not know good? He said: Then say only what you know. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym; Hammam alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from al-Harith except with this chain."
"5920","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, both saying: Uthman ibn Matar al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The expiation of a gathering is: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Uthman ibn Matar alone narrated it."
"5921","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: al-Sakan ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from al-Walid Abu Hashim, from Farqad Abu Talhah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Janab who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urging for the army of hardship; Uthman ibn Affan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, upon me are one hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of Allah. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while upon the pulpit saying: No harm upon Uthman for what he does after this. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Janab except with this chain; Sakan ibn al-Mughirah alone narrated it."
"5922","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yala Zanbur narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Nafi, from his father, from Umm Salamah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Qunut in the night prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yala Zanbur alone narrated it."
"5923","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A cow suffices for seven, and a camel for seven. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Sad except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"5924","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Yala al-Tawwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, greeted him, and he gestured to me. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah, from Ibn Masud, except Muhammad ibn Sirin, and no one from Ibn Sirin except Hisham, and no one from Hisham except Ibn Raja; Abu Yala al-Tawwazi alone narrated it."
"5925","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the sun eclipsed at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them: he recited a long chapter, then bowed five bowings and prostrated twice, then stood for the second, recited a long chapter, then bowed five bowings, then prostrated twice, then sat as he was facing the qiblah supplicating until its eclipse cleared. No one narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that in the eclipse there are ten bowings in four prostrations, except Ubayy ibn Kab, and it is not narrated from Ubayy ibn Kab except with this chain; Abu Jafar al-Razi alone narrated it."
"5926","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever carries the four sides of the bier, Allah expiates forty major sins from him. This hadith is not narrated from Anas ibn Malik except with this chain; Ali ibn Abi Sarah alone narrated it, and none narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Anas ibn Malik."
"5927","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity on green vegetables. None joined this hadith from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, except Ata ibn al-Saib, and none narrated it connected from Ata except al-Harith ibn Nabhan; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari alone narrated it."
"5928","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in good so long as he does not hasten. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he hasten? He said: He says: I supplicated my Lord and He did not answer me."
"5929","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us except saying: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"5930","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dishonors Quraysh, Allah will dishonor him before his death. No one narrated these hadiths from Qatadah except Abu Hilal."
"5931","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu Matar, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the sound of thunder, would say: O Allah, do not destroy us with anything of Your punishment, and grant us health before that. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Abu Matar, and no one from Abu Matar except al-Hajjaj; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad alone narrated it."
"5932","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bewitched, so he supplicated his Lord, then said: Did you not know that Allah Almighty answered me? Two angels came to me; one sat at my head and the other at my feet. One said to the other: What ails the man? He said: Bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-Asam the Jew. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and hair in the sheath of a date-palm at the well of Banu Raysan beneath the rock. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, go to it; its water is like infusion. I wanted to drain it, but he said: Allah has healed me. No one narrated this hadith from Murajja ibn Raja except Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi."
"5933","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Tammam ibn Bazigh narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor our elder and have mercy on our young. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Mubarak ibn Fudalah; Sahl ibn Tammam ibn Bazigh alone narrated it."
"5934","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Musa ibn Ismail al-Tabudhaki narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Zurarah ibn Karim ibn al-Harith ibn Amr al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather al-Harith: that he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was upon his she-camel al-Adba. He said: I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: May Allah forgive you. Then I turned from the other side hoping he would single me out, and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: May Allah forgive you. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what about Fara and Atirah? He said: Whoever wishes may offer Fara, whoever wishes may offer Atirah, and whoever wishes may not offer Atirah; and for sheep, its sacrifice. Then he said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you like the sacredness of this day of yours in this month of yours. This hadith is not narrated from al-Harith ibn Amr except from the hadith of his son with this chain; Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated it from Utbah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Sahmi, from Karim ibn al-Harith, from his father."
"5935","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Amr, the freed slave of Anbasah, narrated to us, from Raitah bint Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali who said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, order your women not to pray unadorned, even if with a necklace of string. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Qays ibn al-Rabi alone narrated it."
"5936","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Hubayrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept while sitting until he snored, then stood and prayed without performing ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath, from Abu Hubayrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, except Sharik; others narrated it from Ashath, from Abu Hubayrah, from Said ibn Jubayr."
"5937","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr al-Asadi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hesitated over a verse in the dawn prayer; when he finished the prayer he turned to the people with his face and said: Did Ubayy ibn Kab attend the prayer with you? They said: No. He said: The people thought he only missed him so he could prompt him. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Qays ibn al-Rabi alone narrated it."
"5938","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, both saying: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Majishun narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from his grandmother Rumaythah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if I wished I could have kissed the place of the seal from him due to my closeness, I would have done so, while he was saying: The Throne of the Merciful shook when he died, meaning thereby Sad ibn Muadh. This hadith is not narrated from Rumaythah except with this chain; Yusuf al-Majishun alone narrated it."
"5939","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Suhaym al-Bahili narrated to us, from Ibn Awn who said: I wrote to Nafi asking him about supplication before fighting, and he wrote to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq, killed their fighters and took their offspring captive; Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated that to me, and he was in that army. None transmitted with a chain from Ali ibn Suhaym al-Bahili, a Basran, other than this hadith; Abu al-Walid alone narrated it."
"5940","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and we brought out for him a brass vessel; he performed ablution, washed his face three times, his forearms twice twice, wiped his head moving his hands forward and back. None said in this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Zayd: we brought out for him a brass vessel, except al-Majishun."
"5941","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Shabur, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah who said: We entered upon Salman, and he called for what was in the house, saying: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from burdening ourselves for a guest, I would have burdened myself for you. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Shabur except Qays ibn al-Rabi."
"5942","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nuaym narrated to me, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) measured a span for Fatimah from her heel, a span, and said: This is the train of a woman. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Mutamir; Dirar ibn Surad alone narrated it."
"5943","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the word of Allah Almighty: Not equal are those of the believers who sit, other than those with harm. Ibn Abbas said: They are people held back by pains or illnesses; those are the ones with harm, and the sick sitter is more excused than the healthy sitter. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Nadrah except Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi Bashir ibn Uqbah."
"5944","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni and Yunus ibn Musa al-Shami narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Salamah ibn Wahram narrated to me, from Mayl bint Mishrah who said: I saw my father trim his nails then bury them, saying: O my daughter, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing likewise. This hadith is not narrated from Mishrah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul alone narrated it."
"5945","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muawiyah al-Karabi si narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restricted the property of Muadh ibn Jabal and sold it for a debt upon him. No one narrated this hadith connected from Mamar except Hisham ibn Yusuf; Ibrahim ibn Muawiyah alone narrated it."
"5946","5940 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: al-Tayyib ibn Salman narrated to us, he said: I heard Amrah say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer and sits in his prayer place until the sun rises, then prays four rak'ahs, Allah forgives him his sins."
"5947","5941 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: al-Tayyib ibn Salman narrated to us, he said: I heard Amrah say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O believing women, exchange gifts even if with a sheep's trotter, for it strengthens love and removes grudges. No one narrated these two hadiths from Amrah bint Artah - and she is al-Adawiyyah, a Basran, and she is not Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman - except al-Tayyib ibn Salman al-Mu'addib, whose kunyah is Abu Hudhayfah, a trustworthy Basran."
"5948","5942 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to refrain from seeking forgiveness for the people of major sins, until we heard our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have stored my intercession for the people of major sins of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection, so we refrained from much of what was in ourselves, and we hoped for them. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani except Harb ibn Surayj; Shayban was alone in transmitting it."
"5949","5943 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Humran ibn Aban, from Uthman ibn Affan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on one who is easy in buying, easy in paying, easy in demanding payment. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah other than Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman."
"5950","5944 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Talut narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Hanbal ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hirmas except with this chain; Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim al-Bazzar was alone in transmitting it."
"5951","5945 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Waqid, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Seek refuge with Allah from the evil eye, for it is real. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salamah except Abu Waqid Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah; Wuhayb was alone in transmitting it."
"5952","5946 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Waqid, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off (the hand) for a shield worth five dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Waqid except Wuhayb, and it is not narrated from Sa'd except with this chain."
"5953","5947 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Waqid, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever attends a ruler, let him speak good or be silent. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Waqid except Wuhayb."
"5954","5948 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far informed us, from Awf, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you, so he returned it to him, then he sat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten, then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, so he returned it to him, then he sat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twenty, then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, so he returned it to him, then he sat, and he said: Thirty good deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Ja'far; Muhammad ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except with this chain."
"5955","5949 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were around the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and said: Peace be upon you, so the Prophet (upon him peace) said: Ten good deeds, then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, so the Prophet (upon him peace) said: Twenty, then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, so the Prophet (upon him peace) said: Thirty good deeds."
"5956","5950 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand toward a trunk before the pulpit was made; when the pulpit was made, the trunk moaned until we heard its moaning, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand on it and it calmed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sulayman ibn Kathir."
"5957","5951 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: My eyes became inflamed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me during the inflammation, and said: O Zayd, if your eyes were gone because of what afflicts them, what would you do? He said: I would be patient and seek the reward, he said: O Zayd, if your eyes were gone because of what afflicts them, and you were patient and sought the reward, there would be no reward for you except Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except his son Yunus; Abu Qutaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"5958","5952 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and heard a caller say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, so he said: Upon the fitrah, then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he said: He has come out of the Fire, so the people rushed to him, and behold it was a shepherd whose sheep were present when the prayer came so he called the adhan."
"5959","5953 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'la al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm is better than the believer who does not mix with people nor endure their harm. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Abu Ya'la al-Tawzi was alone in transmitting it."
"5960","5954 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flock. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid except Sufyan; al-Ramadi was alone in transmitting it."
"5961","5955 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'n al-Raqqashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us, so he said: Indeed Allah is the Pricer, I hope to meet Allah with none of you demanding from me a wrong in religion or worldly matters. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Abd al-A'la, and it is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain."
"5962","5956 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Sulayman, the muezzin of the mosque of Thabit al-Bunani, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness at night to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Dawud ibn Sulayman; his son Sulayman was alone in transmitting it."
"5963","5957 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord for the heedless among the offspring of mankind, and He gave them to me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Fudayl ibn Sulayman; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mutawakkil was alone in transmitting it."
"5964","5958 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Bilal ibn Abi Burdah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, that al-Hajjaj wanted to entrust to him the judgeship of Basra, so Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks judgeship and seeks help for it is entrusted to himself, and whoever does not seek it nor seek help for it, Allah sends down an angel to guide him. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi was alone in transmitting it."
"5965","5959 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, he said: Nafi' Abu Hurmuz narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Three men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the first said: Peace be upon you, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, then the second came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, and the third came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him: And upon you, while the father of the youth was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah, you added for so-and-so and so-and-so, but did not add anything for my son? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We found nothing more for him, so we returned to him what he said. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Nafi' Abu Hurmuz; Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"5966","5960 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Yahya, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A son was born to Sulayman ibn Dawud, so he said to the devils: Where shall we hide him from death? They said: We will take him to the east, he said: Death will reach him, they said: Then to the west, he said: Death will reach him, they said: To the seas, he said: It will reach him, they said: We will place him between the heaven and the earth, and the angel of death descended upon him and said: O son of Dawud, I was commanded to seize a soul which I sought in the east but did not find, and sought in the west but did not find, and sought in the seas, and sought in the depths of the earths but did not find, then while I was ascending I found it, so I seized it, and his body came until it fell upon his throne, and this is the saying of Allah Almighty: {And We tested Sulayman and placed upon his throne a body, then he repented}. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Yahya ibn Kathir; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"5967","5961 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Aslam al-Kufi narrated to us, from Murrah al-Tayyib, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No body nourished from the unlawful enters Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd was alone in transmitting it."
"5968","5962 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ziyad say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Does he who raises his head before the imam not fear - or: fear - that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey. Abdillah ibn Yunus ibn Ubayd did not attribute any hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd other than this; I heard Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar say: I heard Abdillah ibn Yunus ibn Ubayd say: My father died while I was in my mother's womb."
"5969","5963 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Hammad al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I was watering two men from a leather bucket before me, then I spat and my spittle hit my garment, so I began washing my garment from the bucket before me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ammar, your spittle and your tears are only like the water in your bucket, you only wash your garment from urine, feces, semen with the greater water, and blood and vomit. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Ali ibn Zayd; Thabit ibn Hammad was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ammar ibn Yasir except with this chain."
"5970","5964 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he made us rest with a rest at the end of the night, then we woke with the sun risen, so he said: Depart, depart, so we departed until when the sun was in the middle of the sky he dismounted, and ordered Bilal who called the adhan, and each man of us prayed two rak'ahs, then he led us in prayer, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we repeat it tomorrow at its time? He said: Allah has forbidden usury yet accepts it from us? No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Rashid except Kathir ibn Yahya."
"5971","5965 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar al-Barra narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdillah ibn Babayh, from Abdillah ibn Umar, that al-Jarud Abu al-Mundhir informed him, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stray animals, so he said: The stray of the Muslim is the fuel of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id, nor from al-Muthanna except Abu Ma'shar al-Barra; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari was alone in transmitting it."
"5972","5966 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Dinar informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came, the ugliest of people in face, the ugliest of people in clothes, the foulest of people in smell, coarse and rude, so he stepped over people's necks and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Who created you? He said: Allah, he said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah, he said: Who created the earth? He said: Allah, he said: Who created Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, twice, and held his forehead, then the man stood and left, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the man, so we sought him, as if he had never been, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Iblis, he came to cast doubt upon you in your religion."
"5973","5967 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Dinar informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: In Makkah there were two crippled persons, who had a young son, and when morning came he would carry them and bring them to the mosque, and he would earn for them his day, then when evening came he would carry them and bring them back, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and asked about him, and said: Their son has died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If anyone were to be left for anyone, the son of the two crippled would have been left. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abdillah ibn Dinar except Abdillah ibn Ja'far; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari was alone in transmitting them."
"5974","5968 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakka'i informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Bilal narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah Almighty, so when you see that, hasten to prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Bilal except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except Yazid; Ziyad ibn Abdillah was alone in transmitting it."
"5975","5969 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Musa al-Hadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said: Jabir Abu al-Wazi' narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man had dirhams in his lap distributing them, and another remembers Allah, the one remembering Allah is better. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Umar ibn Musa was alone in transmitting it."
"5976","5970 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Yunus Abu Umayyah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub and Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub and Khalid except Wuhayb."
"5977","5971 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Yunus al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is appointed only to be followed, when he says takbir say takbir, and do not say takbir until he says takbir, and when he bows bow, and do not bow until he bows, and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise, and when he prostrates prostrate, and do not prostrate until he prostrates, and when he raises his head raise, and do not raise until he raises, and if he prays sitting pray sitting all together."
"5978","5972 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Talhah ibn al-Nadr al-Huddani, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin, a man asked him about forgetfulness, so he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a daytime prayer, and that he prayed two rak'ahs then gave salam, so the hasty people left and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened? Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar but they feared to speak to him, so a man among the Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: It was neither shortened nor did I forget, so a man said: By my father and mother, you forgot, you only prayed two rak'ahs, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true? They said: He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah, so he stood and prayed two rak'ahs added to his first two, then gave salam, then prostrated two prostrations similar to his prostration in his prayer, or longer. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Nadr al-Huddani except Ali ibn Nasr and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani."
"5979","5973 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to marry a woman along with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam, nor from Hammam except Muhammad ibn Bilal; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari was alone in transmitting it."
"5980","5974 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Muhammad al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When Allah sent Adam down to the earth, he stood facing the Ka'bah and prayed two rak'ahs, so Allah inspired him with this supplication: O Allah, You know my secret and my open, so accept my excuse, and You know my need so give me my request, and You know what is in myself so forgive me my sin, O Allah, I ask You for faith that touches my heart, and true certainty so that I know that nothing befalls me except what You wrote for me, and contentment with what You apportioned for me, so Allah revealed to him: O Adam, I have accepted your repentance and forgiven your sin, and no one will call upon Me with this supplication except I forgive his sin, suffice him the important matter of his affair, drive Satan away from him, trade for him behind every trader, and the world will come to him humbled even if he does not want it. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Mu'adh ibn Muhammad; al-Nadr ibn Tahir was alone in transmitting it."
"5981","5975 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend your dead, close the eyes, for sight follows the soul, and speak good, for the angels say amen to what the family of the deceased says. This hadith is not narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws except with this chain; Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd was alone in transmitting it."
"5982","5976 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Talut narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ayyub, from al-Jahm ibn Fudalah al-Bahili, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wrongdoer will come on the Day of Resurrection until when he is on the bridge of Hell between darkness and roughness, the wronged one meets him and recognizes him and recognizes what he wronged him with, and those who were wronged will keep taking from those who wronged until they strip what is in their hands of good deeds, and if they have no good deeds, there will come upon them from their evil deeds equal to what they wronged, until they are brought to the lowest depth of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Husayn al-Mu'allim; Ibn Abi Adi was alone in transmitting it."
"5983","5977 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Abi Dubayy narrated to us, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Mihjan, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye clings to a man by Allah's permission until he climbs a high place then falls from it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Daylam ibn Ghazwan was alone in transmitting it."
"5984","5978 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Abi Dubayy narrated to us, from Abu Harb or Abu al-Tufayl, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey with a man before him looking whether there was anything on the road the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would dislike, to remove it from him, when he found an old woman not covering nakedness, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has shaded you, so she turned away, and he said to her three times, each time she turned away from him, she said: What do you command me if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has shaded me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard her saying and said: Turn away from her, for she is arrogant. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Tufayl except with this chain; Daylam ibn Ghazwan was alone in transmitting it."
"5985","5979 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says on the Day of Resurrection: My servant asked you for food and you did not feed him, had you fed him you would have fed Me, and My servant asked you for drink and you did not give him drink, had you given him drink you would have given Me drink. No one narrated this hadith from Sallam ibn Miskin except Talut ibn Abbad."
"5986","5980 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Firas Abu Hurayrah al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Usayd ibn Abi Usayd narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would one of you like his beloved to be adorned with a bracelet of fire? They said: No, he said: Then do not adorn with gold, but play with silver as you play. No one narrated this hadith [with a broken chain in the source]."
"5987","5981 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn al-Nadr al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Kharijah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Sa'd, that some people complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lack of rain, so he said: Kneel on your knees and say: O Lord, O Lord, and he raised the forefinger to the sky, so they did, and they were given rain until they wished it be removed from them. This hadith is not narrated from Sa'd except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi was alone in transmitting it."
"5988","5982 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Talut narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hassan al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Haytham ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, make me fear You as if I see You forever until I meet You, and make me happy with Your piety, and do not make me wretched with Your disobedience, and choose for me in Your decree, and bless for me in Your ordainment so that I do not love hastening what You delayed nor delaying what You hastened, and make my richness in myself, and let me enjoy my hearing and sight, and make them the inheritors from me, and help me against him who wronged me, and show me my vengeance in him, and cool my eye with that. This hadith is not narrated from Irak ibn Malik except with this chain; Ammar ibn Talut was alone in transmitting it."
"5989","5983 - Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Sabuni al-Basri narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plastering graves and building over them and sitting on them. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Adi ibn al-Fadl."
"5990","5984 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When prayer came in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man would hasten to the road and call: Prayer, prayer, so that was hard on people, so they said: If we took a bell, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That is for Christians, they said: If we took a horn? He said: That is for Jews, he said: So Bilal was ordered to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd. No one narrated this hadith in full from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i was alone in transmitting it."
"5991","5985 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding leopard skins."
"5992","5986 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that when the death of the Negus reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him, so he stood and prayed over him with people behind him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Mahbub ibn al-Hasan."
"5993","5987 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, they are the most tender-hearted, faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"5994","5988 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pride and arrogance are among the owners of horses and camels, and dignity and tranquility are among the owners of sheep, and the loud-voiced are the people of fur. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Maryam, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, except Yahya ibn al-Mundhir."
"5995","5989 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyash al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Habib al-Qadi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you to make nabidh in vessels; vessels neither permit anything nor forbid it, so make nabidh in whatever seems to you, and avoid every intoxicant. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Umar ibn Habib."
"5996","5990 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has the world as his concern and grief, for it he rises and it he intends, Allah Almighty places poverty between his eyes, scatters his affair, and nothing of it comes to him except what was written for him, and whoever has the Hereafter as his concern and grief, for it he rises and it he intends, Allah Almighty places richness in his heart, gathers his affair, and the world comes to him humbled. No one narrated this hadith from Hammam except Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi was alone in transmitting it."
"5997","5991 - Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Hatim al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when I was eight years old, so my mother took me to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men and women of the Ansar have given you gifts except me, and I found nothing to gift you except this son of mine, so accept him from me to serve you as long as you wish, he said: So I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years, and he never struck me a blow, nor abused me, nor frowned in my face. The first thing he advised me was saying: O my son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer, and I never informed anyone of his secret at all, and my mother and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me, but I did not inform them of his secret, nor will I ever inform anyone of his secret. Then he said: O my son, perform ablution fully and your life will increase and your two guardians will love you, then he said: O my son, if you can not spend a night except upon ablution then do, for whoever death comes to him while upon ablution is given martyrdom. Then he said: O my son, if you can keep praying then do, for the angels keep praying for you as long as you pray, then he said: O my son, beware of turning in prayer, for turning in prayer is destruction, and if it must be then in voluntary not obligatory. Then he said to me: O my son, when you bow place your palms on your knees, spread your fingers, and lift your hands from your sides, and when you raise your head from bowing settle every limb in its place, for Allah does not look on the Day of Resurrection at him who does not straighten his back, then he said to me: O my son, when you prostrate do not peck as the rooster pecks, nor squat as the dog squats, nor spread your forearms on the ground like the beast, and spread the back of your feet on the ground, and place your buttocks on your heels, for that is easier for you on the Day of Resurrection in your reckoning. Then he said to me: O my son, be thorough in washing from janabah, you will come out of your washing with no sin or fault upon you, I said: By my father and mother, what is thoroughness in washing? He said: Wet the roots of hair and clean the skin. Then he said to me: O my son, if you can make part of your prayer in your house then do, for it increases the goodness of your house, then he said to me: O my son, when you enter upon your family give salam, it will be blessing upon you and your household, then he said to me: O my son, when you leave your family let not your sight fall upon anyone of the people of qiblah except you greet him, you will return with your good deeds increased. Then he said: O my son, if you can enter morning and evening with no deceit in your heart for anyone then do, then he said to me: O Anas, when you leave your family let not your sight fall upon anyone of the people of qiblah except you think he has merit over you, then do. Then he said to me: O my son, that is from my sunnah, and whoever revives my sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise. Then he said to me: O my son, if you keep my advice nothing will be more beloved to you than death. No one narrated this hadith in full from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Ali ibn Zayd, nor from Ali ibn Zayd except Abdillah ibn al-Muthanna; Muslim ibn Hatim was alone in transmitting it, from al-Ansari, from his father, and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid was alone in transmitting it, from Abbad al-Minqari."
"5998","5992 - Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two circumambulations whose performer is forgiven sins however great: a circumambulation after morning prayer ending at sunrise, and a circumambulation after Asr ending at sunset, they said: O Messenger of Allah, if before that and after? He said: It is joined to it. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except Zayd al-Ammi."
"5999","5993 - Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, he said: Mahan ibn Sirah Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Burd narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant whose fire is not extinguished, whose worms do not die, nor his punishment lightened: he who associates with Allah, and a man who drags a man to a ruler without sin and he kills him, and a man who disobeys his parents. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Asim ibn Mihja' was alone in transmitting it."
"6000","5994 - Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abdillah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ru'asi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man from Banu Kilab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the stud fee of a stallion, so he forbade him, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, we lend the stallion and are honored, so he permitted him in the honorarium."
